{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/865489-crossover-concept-detective-agency","id":865489,"title":"Crossover Concept - Detective Agency","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-14T07:29:18-07:00","id":865489,"title":"Crossover Concept - Detective Agency","content":"So, this is a topic for assembling &quot;Detective&quot; archetype character ideas into a multi-supernatural detective agency. All the game-lines have the ability to make such characters, though some work better/easier than others. Please post any detective characters you have played or can think up - either geared towards the role, or playing against type. Or interesting cases, or interactions, or anything related, really. <hr /><br /> Long ago, the Arisen Ishaq, of the Sesha-Hebsu, He of the Piercing Gaze, Hunter of Secrets, who declared the primacy of his Ren before Bastu, fell in love with using fine details to uncover the deepest mysteries and bring judgement upon those who thought they've escaped justice . He even restructured his cult, now the Association of the Illuminated Eye, to uncover details about various mysteries and cases in between his Descents, waking him when they encounter particularly hard or dangerous cases. His cult/business has seen a boom in growth in recent years, ever since he hired Evelyn Friday (A.K.A., Ms. Friday, a Messenger/Inquisitor) to handle secretarial work and contract negotiation, and has been branching out into wider supernatural concerns.<br /> <br /> They're now hiring - apply within.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-26-2016, 12:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T04:23:44-07:00","id":868314,"title":"","content":"Here's another one: <hr /><br /> <u><b>Gabrielle Cassidy</b></u> (Werewolf, Irraka, Iron Masters)<br /> &quot;Gabby&quot; was one of those reporters that her interviewees like least to see - appearing out of no where, recorder and/or camera handy, and asking uncomfortable questions. It didn't help that her targets of choice almost always had something to hide. Despite her incisive exposes and editorials, her career took a dive after some of her investigations into the city's big names turned up nothing, giving her the nickname of &quot;Cries Wolf&quot; amongst her peers. Bouncing from paper to paper, she seemed destined for tabloids when she tried to accuse a wealthy philanthropist of some kind of human blood trafficking. After sneaking out in the dark of night under the new moon to investigate an old factory she believed was a distribution point, she was captured and tied up. And underwent her First Change, escaping her bonds and hunting down everyone in the factory. Though there was some blood, police never found any bodies, nor sign of much struggle, leaving the incident destined for their cold case files. For Gabby, she's merely found new ways to &quot;hunt&quot; for the Truth by joining the IE Detective Agency.<br /> <br /> <b>Concepts and Ideas</b>: Werewolf Investigative Reporter/Detective. Totem acting as an immaterial &quot;Watson&quot;. Uses Irraka Siskur Dah Condition (Unaware) to prime her targets for surprise interviews.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-19-2016, 10:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T07:14:59-07:00","id":870166,"title":"","content":"Anybody have any suggestions for Beast? Or variant suggestions for Mage or Changeling (because the basic concept is so easily a detective, what about one that plays against type, like an Ogre or Obrimos)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T18:04:11-07:00","id":871936,"title":"","content":"Hope you don't mind if throw this out there...<br /> <br /> <b>Maria Katsaros</b> (Beast, Anakim Nemesis)<br /> Maria's childhood was an unhappy one; her parents were loving but poor, working three and a half jobs between them to make ends meet, leaving little time for her and her siblings. It didn't help that other children were always cruel, because of their lack of money, and her unusual height. Not even the most well-meaning teachers or priests could protect a girl who topped six feet by the time she was fourteen, and in her school, well-meaning teachers were few and far between. More than one authority figure joined her classmates in muttering about her &quot;freakishness,&quot; not knowing (or not caring) how good her hearing was. In her junior year of high school, she walked straight from a brutal tongue-lashing by the principal to interrupting a group of bullies beating up her younger brother. She snapped, leaped on them in a fury, and was beaten unconscious herself for the trouble. <br /> <br /> When the unconsciousness slipped into sleep, she had the dream again, the dream of the monster who whispered secrets into her ear even as it hunted her; it was the last time she would have that dream, or any other. She realized the monster had been herself all along, and awoke in the hospital bed, the Horror looking out of her eyes. Shortly after that, those bullies never bothered anyone again. Maria finished high school, putting on muscle and curves as the rest of her body caught up with her height, and joined the police academy; it seemed like a perfect positive outlet for her Hunger to Punish those who harmed children. It worked out well for a few years, until she let her emotions get the better of her one too many times, and was fired for police brutality. Fortunately, the IE Detective Agency is always on the lookout for new talent. For the first time in her life, she finally feels at home.<br /> <br /> In the waking world, Maria is a six-foot-three amazon with smooth olive skin and warm Mediterranean features. Her Horror is a massive, yet disturbingly graceful giantess, with razor claws and three heads upon her broad shoulders; those of a she-wolf, tigress, and eagle. Maria is a valued asset to the Agency for her tremendous strength, keen senses, contacts on the force, and grateful devotion to her newfound family.... though her enemies from her days on the Force haven't forgotten her either.<br /> <br /> <b>Concepts:</b> Giant avenger of the small, the heavy. Priority Atavisms are Cyclopean Strength and Needs Must. Likely to develop Kinship Nightmares based on other detectives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T05:37:56-07:00","id":872296,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1419_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1419\" data-vbnamecard=\"1419\">WarDragon</a> Thanks for that. How well do you think she'd get along with the secretary? (As, according to fluff, Unchained and Begotten aren't supposed to mesh well)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T16:11:39-07:00","id":872704,"title":"","content":"(I kinda went way overboard with this, but when I saw a request for a non-obvious changeling investigator I decided to rise to the challenge. Didn't go with an Ogre though.)<br /> <br /> <u><b>George \u201cWash\u201d Zeghers</b></u> (Changeling: Beast Oni/Author)<br /> <br /> \u201c<i>I got the pictures.\u201d He says, softly. \u201cFound the honest-to-god truth, just like you wanted, just like you paid for. Don't shoot the messenger.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> Wash pretends to hate his job. He sighs often, chews his bottom lip constantly, and never seems to be able to meet the eyes of his more desperate clients. He pretends to be a man near the end of his rope, worn down by years in the business. He looks the part as well. Receding black hair above hollow eyes above thin, slack, lips and weeks-unkempt beard.<br /> <br /> His Mien tells a different story. Wash is a changeling, who cares for the truth above laws or feelings, who does what he does because he does it better than anyone else. Greater truths aren't his concern. No corruption or conspiracies draw his attention, just people being lied to by those they trust. A wild midnight mane encircles his pale and wrinkled face. His skin is gray and patched with brush-strokes, like a water-color painting. His eyes are large, dark, and hungry, and his stretched smile barely contains a mouthful of tusks and fangs.<br /> <br /> Wash's story started with a claims adjustment, the part of his job that used to be his specialty. A car accident led to a hospital room that led to a durance spent as a guardian lion sitting at the feet of a blind and deformed god. Wash would watch scenes of madness and sorrow unfold in front of him and then whisper them into his master's ears to keep him entertained. The only grotesqueries the keeper could not abide, were the facts of his own appearance. As the fae covered his ears and wailed in defiance of the truth, Wash made good his escape.<br /> <br /> Some people would call what Wash does now stalking, though he just considers himself a truth-seeker. Whenever a paranoid spouse or suspicious employer comes looking for a background check, looking for dirt, Wash does \u201chis best\u201d to convince them that the truth isn't always pretty, isn't always worth it. More often than not, they don't listen. So he takes his camera and goes to work. He asks questions and takes photos, artistically incriminated, but never wholly untrue. He paints a picture, tells a story. The truth in its barest, ugliest form. People don't like what they see. They cry, or scream, or shout, and Wash grows stronger. He never feels sorry for it. What he does isn't wrong. After all, they asked for it.<br /> <br /> <b>Relationships:</b><br /> <br /> Ishaq:<i> He's been on this job longer than anyone. And I mean anyone. He has a lot of stories to tell, a lot to teach, when he can keep all the details straight.</i><br /> <br /> Friday: <i>We don't talk much. She always gets straight to the point, doesn't mince words, and then she's off again. I think maybe she should cut loose sometimes, but I can respect her dedication to the job</i>.<br /> <br /> Gabby:<i> I really relate to her. A wild animal, a nosy nuisance, a girl after my own heart. She's a good kid. I keep having to remind myself that she's not my kid. She doesn't need me looking after her.</i><br /> <br /> Maria: <i>PI's usually work for the defense, so it's a bit awkward sometimes to have a cop hanging around. She's saved my pelt more times than I can count on one hand though, so I can look past it.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Concepts</b>: Brutally honest PI. Takes great pride in his photography and narrative. Contracts probably include Fang and Talon (senses) and Discreet Conjuration. Dual-Kith merit, obviously. Mien and Seeming blessing probably involve being inappropriately honest or blunt.<br /> <br /> (I might make another one of these...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1063-kajedhorrors","name":"kajedhorrors","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T17:06:50-07:00","id":872741,"title":"","content":"Hard to say for sure without knowing more about Ms. Friday, but it probably depends a lot on who won the initial detection/dominance roll-off. If Maria won, or if they tied, then Ms. Friday probably does a bunch of little passive-aggressive things to mess with her, doing whatever she can to cover her fear short of naked hostility or hindering investigations. If Friday won, then Maria's probably scared as hell of whatever dirt the demon's got on her.<br /> <br /> It's... probably best if they avoid each other when at all possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T19:19:46-07:00","id":872811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/865489-crossover-concept-detective-agency?p=870166#post870166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anybody have any suggestions for Beast? Or variant suggestions for Mage or Changeling (because the basic concept is so easily a detective, what about one that plays against type, like an Ogre or Obrimos)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I got a tentative concept for a Vampire, as well as for a Changeling who specializes in locating magical phenomena. Names may be subject to change....<br /> <br /> * <b>Amado Tejera </b>- Columbian, Male (Gangrel, Les Gens Libres Bloodline, Ordo Dracul)<br /> * <b>Susan Malloy </b>- Irish American, Female (Changeling, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1elqCKhNJweqnLuUy8Rbh2PiZSsnccnXQWrNy8cPf5o4/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Spelldrinker</a>)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T08:02:16-07:00","id":873760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WarDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/865489-crossover-concept-detective-agency?p=872741#post872741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hard to say for sure without knowing more about Ms. Friday, but it probably depends a lot on who won the initial detection/dominance roll-off. If Maria won, or if they tied, then Ms. Friday probably does a bunch of little passive-aggressive things to mess with her, doing whatever she can to cover her fear short of naked hostility or hindering investigations. If Friday won, then Maria's probably scared as hell of whatever dirt the demon's got on her.<br /> <br /> It's... probably best if they avoid each other when at all possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ms. Friday's personality is... dynamic. She changes it depending on the audience, the context, and her purpose. Externally, at least. Internally, amongst the rest of the Agency, she's &quot;strictly professional&quot; - clear cut, to the point, helpful but not quite friendly. The only one she seems to display some real affection for is Ishaq, whom she dotes on as a forgetful uncle. Regarding Maria, they probably do engage in petty aggravations due to unease, but nothing besides that due to professionalism (on Friday's side, at least), and &quot;family&quot; (for Maria's side). Probably a situation of &quot;you might not like them, but you can respect them and you are on the same side&quot;.<br /> <br /> Ishaq's personality can be summed up as &quot;absent-minded/forgetful veteran of his craft&quot;. He's full of old stories and pointers (when he can remember them), and he looks at each member as a combination of valued employee, protege, and nephew/niece. The &quot;absent minded&quot; part gets dropped when he focuses on a mystery of his own, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-25-2016, 03:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T08:50:16-07:00","id":873790,"title":"","content":"<b>Ms. Morte</b><br /> Mage, Moros, Free Council<br /> Consultant Coroner<br /> <br /> <i>She removes her rubber gloves with a snap, not even bothering to touch the body. &quot;Double shot from a small-caliber handgun to the back of the head. Mob caught up with her for fleecing their gambling den and denning the boss' daughter. I thought I told you not to bother me with this small-time stuff?&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Any good detective agency needs quality contacts, and Ms. Morte is one of them. Really, she's a three-for-one: her day job as a police coroner gets her lots of access to open cases, her role in the local Concilium gives an in for Supernal goings-on, and her boredom with both means she'll work freelance for the agency. It's hard to keep her attention, and she downplays her interest in any case, but her expertise with bodies and the dead means she's indispensable for those times when the corpses just start piling up. Just don't ask her about Spirits. Really don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","user":"AceOfAlmonds","date":". 04-25-2016, 12:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T18:50:48-07:00","id":874163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/865489-crossover-concept-detective-agency?p=873760#post873760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ms. Friday's personality is... dynamic. She changes it depending on the audience, the context, and her purpose. Externally, at least. Internally, amongst the rest of the Agency, she's &quot;strictly professional&quot; - clear cut, to the point, helpful but not quite friendly. The only one she seems to display some real affection for is Ishaq, whom she dotes on as a forgetful uncle. Regarding Maria, they probably do engage in petty aggravations due to unease, but nothing besides that due to professionalism (on Friday's side, at least), and &quot;family&quot; (for Maria's side). Probably a situation of &quot;you might not like them, but you can respect them and you are on the same side&quot;.<br /> <br /> Ishaq's personality can be summed up as &quot;absent-minded/forgetful veteran of his craft&quot;. He's full of old stories and pointers (when he can remember them), and he looks at each member as a combination of valued employee, protege, and nephew/niece. The &quot;absent minded&quot; part gets dropped when he focuses on a mystery of his own, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds about right; Maria can be plenty professional (well, depending on how Hungry she is at the moment). Though the &quot;family&quot; part would be more out of respect for &quot;Uncle&quot; Ishaq and the other &quot;cousins&quot; in the Agency, not Friday herself. To quote the book, &quot;Demons are <i>not </i>kin.&quot; Ironically, if there's anybody around that she'd suspect of betraying the Agency, it'd be Friday, no matter how likely that actually is.<br /> <br /> Probably knows Ms. Morte from way back, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T02:26:07-07:00","id":874364,"title":"","content":"Has no-one got a Geist character? Because if not, can a place be held for one of mine. They'll probably be a consultant for if the agency has a particularly difficult that necessitates dealing with the ghosts of the victims or entering the Underworld or similar shenanigans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 04-26-2016, 05:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T08:37:09-07:00","id":874569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/865489-crossover-concept-detective-agency?p=874364#post874364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has no-one got a Geist character? Because if not, can a place be held for one of mine. They'll probably be a consultant for if the agency has a particularly difficult that necessitates dealing with the ghosts of the victims or entering the Underworld or similar shenanigans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Feel free - it's not like there is only a 1-character-per-splat rule.<br /> <br /> This also gave me the idea for another related character - but a patron/employer, rather than a member or consultant: A Bonepicker/Advocate that hires the Agency to investigate &quot;cold cases&quot; on behalf of ghosts. Giving back to the community, as it were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T09:13:01-07:00","id":874592,"title":"","content":"Oh, note that Fan-splats are perfectly acceptable/allowed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T13:45:12-07:00","id":874843,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Anton Neville Krausberg</b></u> (Sin-Eater, Stricken, Advocate (former Bonepicker))<br /> Anton grew up in the gutter, constantly on the lookout for any advantage or even his next meal. His story would have ended there, in fact it <i>did</i> end there, one cold, dark night as Anton lay dying of the flu in some alley. But there in the darkness, he made a Bargain. Given a new lease on life and strange powers, Anton resolved to never get stepped on or over again. Dealing with the discarded shades of the departed, he'd found hidden caches of drugs and cash, bought himself some small position and respect, and leverage his &quot;connections&quot; to rise even further. In a few decades, he'd left his life of squalor far behind, undercut his rivals, and made millions. He even &quot;opened&quot; his own casino (after getting the previous tenants/owners convicted of murder). But he never forgot the &quot;friends&quot; who enabled his fortunes. Now in his twilight years, he's determined to give back to the voiceless dead. Anton's vast contacts amongst the more persistent ghosts of the area let him hear about those who've been wronged unto the grave, and beyond. And he's willing to pay the IE Detective Agency to see the dead get their justice.<br /> <br /> <b>Concepts and Ideas</b>: Financier and Advocate for the Dead. Reformed Cut-throat Capitalist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T19:53:06-07:00","id":875157,"title":"","content":"Are hunters acceptable?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T22:49:37-07:00","id":875327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/865489-crossover-concept-detective-agency?p=875157#post875157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are hunters acceptable?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, considering everyone else in the organization is supernatural (practically), how do you think it would work out? I'm not saying no, but that needs to be taken into account.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T03:29:22-07:00","id":875457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/865489-crossover-concept-detective-agency?p=875327#post875327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, considering everyone else in the organization is supernatural (practically), how do you think it would work out? I'm not saying no, but that needs to be taken into account.</div> </div> </div> </div>Im thinking of a hunter that part of two conspiracies actually. The Lucifuge to give him the power to deal with Every ephemeral entity. And be a Field Liaison for Vanguard Serial Crimes Unit, which would allow him to work with a detective agency &quot;legally&quot;. <br /> Both of these conspiracies are actually pretty nice in regards to how they deal with supernaturals. The first because they are monster like themselves and latter because they understand that the &quot;monsters&quot; are still citizens.<br /> As for the benefit of the agency he can arrest people on the spot and VASCU has a prison ment for supernaturals. <br /> I mean without a doubt the agency will eventually deal with supernatural criminal so it be nice to have a way of legally incarcerate those criminals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10820,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","user":"Blakemikizuki","date":". 04-27-2016, 06:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T07:56:13-07:00","id":875637,"title":"","content":"Ms. Morte on the members of the agency:<br /> <br /> Ishaq: <i>He's the biggest mystery in the agency, and yet they never call me in on his case. Shame. I'm certain I could figure out what killed him.</i><br /> <br /> Friday: <i>I can respect not wanting to use your real name, really I can. It's just...girl Friday? Really? I wasn't aware McCarthy was still in office...</i><br /> <br /> Gabby: <i>She's subtle when she's hunting, but very direct when she's got her teeth in someone. Figuratively and literally. </i><br /> <br /> Maria: <i>I still don't understand why she was fired. She was very good at uncovering the nastier truths of this city, and making sure they didn't happen again. She has my complete respect.</i><br /> <br /> Wash: <i>He knows I want the truth. Honestly, he only asks so he can say &quot;I told you so&quot; later. He's so self-satisfied when he gets to, I hate to tell him he's wasting his time.</i><br /> <br /> Anton: <i>Oooh, how does something like you even happen? Do you mind if I talk to your rider?</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Also, fan splats you say... gotta noodle on that, but having an idea for a Princess that may or may not pan out (Tempesta Mender, something like a mob doctor).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T08:22:47-07:00","id":875660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/865489-crossover-concept-detective-agency?p=875457#post875457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Im thinking of a hunter that part of two conspiracies actually. The Lucifuge to give him the power to deal with Every ephemeral entity. And be a Field Liaison for Vanguard Serial Crimes Unit, which would allow him to work with a detective agency &quot;legally&quot;.<br /> Both of these conspiracies are actually pretty nice in regards to how they deal with supernaturals. The first because they are monster like themselves and latter because they understand that the &quot;monsters&quot; are still citizens.<br /> As for the benefit of the agency he can arrest people on the spot and VASCU has a prison ment for supernaturals.<br /> I mean without a doubt the agency will eventually deal with supernatural criminal so it be nice to have a way of legally incarcerate those criminals.</div> </div> </div> </div>How would the dual Conspiracies work? They usually don't like their secrets getting out (and I get the feeling the Lucifuge doesn't really do retirement). It mostly seems like only the VASCU connection is required (but if you can come up with a good story supporting both, feel free).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/865489-crossover-concept-detective-agency?p=875637#post875637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, fan splats you say... gotta noodle on that, but having an idea for a Princess that may or may not pan out (Tempesta Mender, something like a mob doctor).</div> </div> </div> </div>That... could get interesting. As for Fan-splats, I'm working on a &quot;Green Hornet&quot; team, with a Leviathan and an Atoll. Still trying to finalize some details before fleshing out backstory and personalities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T08:55:17-07:00","id":875699,"title":"","content":"Worker Drone 23546-CE5b aka Bill (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1N36xnDtrEWYVRvyLeWdf1AEJxKSrGbAH_CSLsAeXAfY/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Alien,</a> Cimex, Grass\u0101t\u014dr\u0113s)<br /> <br /> To most the homeless man known as Bill is just another figure on the street, sifting through dumpsters and begging for food. A handful of others know that he has an unusually good sense of what's going on in the criminal underworld. Those in the know among the IE Detectives know that's because he understands criminal systems better than anyone else. Give him some names, an address and some sugary snacks for his time and Bill will find out just about anything about any criminal activity in the city.<br /> <br /> See Bill is, like many homeless, from out of town. Unlike many homeless he's from a small star system in the Andromeda Galaxy.<br /> <br /> His species formed into an impossibly rigid caste system of generally known as 'The Hive' where every individual was born into their station and role and everyone is provided with what they will need to live. From the moment he came into this universe Bill knew he was never meant to be anything great, he was a lowly worker drone, unworthy of even a name. He did have an unusual gift for subverting the system, twisting requisitions just enough to get access to things he wasn't supposed to, being in the right place at the wrong time to overhear the education of higher ranked drones, etc. Using his clever tricks he managed to live a life well beyond his approved means. Eventually the Hive grew wary of Bill's antics and he was forced to flee. He made a living doing odd jobs for various crime syndicates across the stars, gaining an understanding that his tricks were not unique to him, every world had criminals that sought to break the rules to better their own lives.<br /> <br /> A little over a decade ago he got struck by a solar flare and crash landed on Earth. On this primitive planet Bill found a society not entirely unlike the Hive. Here the people fumbled around for meaning and direction for most of their lives but when they managed to stumble into their roles they took them with unwavering faith. Those that don't find their fulfilling roles twist and break the rules in ways even Bill hadn't imagined before. He felt horrid pains of nostalgia for his old life and did not want to see this system corrupted and twisted as he had twisted the Hive. He regularly takes on jobs exposing criminal activity for the IE Detective Agency but isn't an official employee for two reasons, one he doesn't legally exist on Earth, two he is genuinely uninterested in money, he's all too happy to be paid in food but does not seem to make the connection that money can be used to purchase food.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9065-darkblade","name":"Darkblade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T11:48:35-07:00","id":875808,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Dr. Jeremiah Jordan Jiller, Consultant Psychologist</u></b> (Genius, Staunen Scholastic)<br /> Jeremiah was always fascinated by the depths of a human mind. People do all sorts of things. People have ambitions. People fall in love. People fall into depression. People commit acts of altruism and good will. People commit crimes. What caused them to this behaviour, though. What made people who they are? What made criminals who they are? How did they reason, how did they think of themselves, what were they driven by, what caused one man to be a vicious murdered and the other to be a paragon of all good and christian values? All of the answers he recieved never satisfied him. He felt like there was more. He decided to, instead of listening to others, find his own answers. And so, after years of meticulous study, he became a crime psychologist. Throught his career, he talked to many various criminals, murderers, thieves, smugglers, forgers. He analyzed the deeds of many more. Over the years, he created many psychological profiles, meticulously analyzing every last bit of them, trying to extract a singular common value. It was not enough. He decided he needed much more information than this, much more than he had. He began to deal with the matters of his criminologist colleagues, to take note of every single detail of the crime scene, compare it with the psychological profile of the perpetrator, and make connections. Bizarre and unjustified, but connections nonetheless. Somewhere in the middle of this, he catalyzed,and didn't even notice until a bit later, when he realized he's took up to engineering and inventing. Some time afterwards, he was privately approached by a worker of the Illuminated Eye, with an offer. Help them as a consultant with whatever they have for him, as a little profitable sidejob to utilize his workaholism for something better, and in exchange, he gets to do anything he wants to before the stuff is turned to the police. He accepted. He'd be a fool not to.<br /> <br /> <b>Concepts and Ideas: </b>Workaholic Mad Psychologist, Taking all he can get to find the defining element of human psyche responsible for criminal behaviour(And, as a matter of fact, any higher behaviour) . I'd imagine he'd use all Apokalypsi he can get, and maybe a bit of Epikrato to make people he talks to be more open when he needs them to.<br /> <br /> Dr. Jiller on other people in the agency:<br /> Ishaq: <i>Tell me, how different were the criminals back in your day? Oh? You don't remember? That's fine, I'll guess I'll just wait...</i><br /> Ms. Friday: <i>A great Machine... That influences the minds of people all around the world, to get what it needs, with no moral qualms whatsoever.. Lead the way!</i><br /> Gabrielle: You're there, always, to tear down the layers of their lies... You wouldn't mind, if I took a look at what's left when you're done?<br /> Maria: <i>You strive to deal punishment, to teach the crooks that crime does not pay off... But how often do they learn? Have you ever wandered how much you change people's lives, people's minds?</i><br /> Wash: <i>You're not looking for truth. You're looking for facts. There's a difference. </i><br /> Ms. Morte: <i>The body tells you nothing about the rest. About the mind, and soul. About the driving force. I wonder how much of you is what you saw up there and how much is actual you?</i><br /> Anton:<i> Are you suuuure you couldn't arrange a talk with Jack the Ripper? No? What about the Scorpio? No? Okay, fine, I'll settle down for John Wilkes Booth.</i> <br /> Bill: <i>Everyone's role, assigned to them, from the very beginning... I wonder how that influences your mindset?</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T10:47:56-07:00","id":881975,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Norwood Edward Hart</b></u> (Mortal, Atoll)<br /> Coming from a distinguished, wealthy (if currently at risk) British family, Norwood has seldom wanted for much. And considering the accomplishments of his forebears, Norwood understands that with these benefits comes certain expectations. He has honed his mind towards the uncovering of secrets, and fancies himself a modern day Sherlock Holmes. Something his short, but impressive record seems to substantiate. Though he is in fairly high demand, he's refused position or employment at most agencies who've contacted him, due to their disrespectful attitude towards his disheveled, but trustworthy assistant Warner Roach. He has accepted tentative employment at the IE Detective Agency due to their tolerance, nay, acceptance of his assistant's unfortunate demeanor.<br /> <br /> In truth, though Norwood is a passably good detective (mostly for his abilities to put clues together once presented with them, and talk people into trusting him with details), he wouldn't be nearly as good as he thinks he is without Warner. Though a staunch defender of Warner and others judged more upon appearance than ability, he is blinded by his own ego and romanticized worldview. He's as unaware of Warner's supernatural nature (or the supernatural in general) as he is of the fact that the Agency wouldn't even have hired him if not for his &quot;assistant&quot;. Despite that, the two do make a good team, especially for cases where Norwood's superlative ability to come up with non-Supernatural explanations and draw attention are required.<br /> <br /> <b>Concepts and Ideas</b>: Self-styled Sherlock Holmes. Self-appointed &quot;White Savior&quot; to the downtrodden. Glory-hound with a good heart. Blinded rationalist.<br /> <br /> <b>Norwood on others</b>:<br /> Ishaq: <i>Fine chap. Knows how to respect his subordinates, and has a grandiosely embellished tale to tell or two. I can see us working well together.</i><br /> Friday: <i>Charming woman. Always knows the right thing to say, and keeps the rest of the office running smoothly. But she treats Warner with respect, which is her true virtue.</i><br /> Gabrielle: <i>An energetic girl, if a tad verbose. She's still one moment, then digging into her target like a terrier. She could be a great detective herself, if she'd listen to some of my advice.</i><br /> Maria: <i>Something about her seems a bit... off. But I respect the work she does to protect children and others who can't protect themselves. I suppose seeing what she has </i>would<i> give her an odd edge.</i><br /> Wash: <i>A man with a fine dedication to his craft (if not his appearance). Committed to the truth, despite how much the listeners might not want to hear it. At least, professionally. He has a dry sense of humour and implies the wildest things about Warner with a straight face.</i><br /> Ms Morte: <i>A very... direct woman. Certainly gifted in her field, the way she can tell cause of death seemingly just by looking at a body. I get the feeling she doesn't think too highly of me, though. But then, not everyone thinks my reputation is earned - I'll just have to prove it to her.</i><br /> Anton: <i>Currently upstanding member of the community. Runs a fine casino. I hear he used to be in the criminal underworld, but nothing was ever proven. Still, he seems very concerned about these Cold Cases he keeps bringing up. I wonder what his sources are?</i><br /> Bill: <i>A very odd fellow with his ear to the ground. He delivers far more than he asks for, which is rare for people in his position. I do wish he'd accept at least a little charity from time to time, but he truly seems to not care about wealth. Astonishing.</i><br /> Dr. Jiller: <i>A fellow scholar and exemplar of the mind, though in a different, </i>denser<i> field. We've had a few conversations about the criminal mind over drinks from time to time, but the liquor seems to hit him harder - it isn't long before he veers off into nonsensibility.</i><br /> <br /> <u><b>Warner Roach</b></u> (Leviathan, Lahamin, School of the Reef)<br /> Warner Roach grew up in fairly depressing circumstances - broken home, poverty, alienated by others. He never let that keep him down though, and always dreamed of doing better and making something of himself. He just... didn't think that something would be some primordial horror. While stumbling around in turmoil, trying to adapt to his new life, he had a chance encounter with Norwood Hart and helped him solve a high profile case. Feeling truly at peace for the first time, and encouraged by Norwood's appreciation for his help, Warner signed on with his hero-figure and used his &quot;abilities&quot; to help him solve many more mysteries. He doesn't mind not getting as much credit - he finally has a place he feels he belongs and can do some good.<br /> <br /> Chance encounters brought Warner into contact with other members of his &quot;family&quot;, who educated him on certain facts of life for the Wicked Tribe. He's taken up the School of the Reef, but has decided to hone his investigatory abilities in the service of Norwood, rather than physical augmentation. He knows what effect the Wake might have when he is separated from Norwood's suppressing influence, though considering Warner is around helping his hero at all hours, this doesn't really change things for Warner much.<br /> <br /> <b>Concepts and Ideas</b>: Humble helper secretly pulling the weight. Kato to Norwood's Green Hornet. Super-effective man-servant and sidekick.<br /> <br /> <b>Warner on others</b>:<br /> Ishaq: <i>Nice guy, especially for someone dead most of the time. He knows what it's like to both have power and still serve.</i><br /> Friday: <i>Nice lady. Talks </i>to<i> me, not </i>at<i> me. Makes sure the checks come on time, too, which helps.</i><br /> Gabrielle: <i>I... don't really know how to talk to her. She does enough for both of us (or anyone), I guess. I just try to smile and nod. I think it's nice, though, that she doesn't say anything about the... you know... smell.</i><br /> Maria: <i>Some people are big on the inside - Maria's both. I like her, but I get the feeling she doesn't think much of Mr. Hart. Guess she doesn't see what I see, then.</i><br /> Wash: <i>I like the stories he tells. Not all the endings, maybe, but he tells it plain. Still, when he asks me if I want to know the Truth about me, I say &quot;no&quot;. I already know some truths I'm not comfortable with.</i><br /> Ms Morte: <i>She seems... nice? Very direct, but kinda bored. I mostly just try to stay out of her way. </i><br /> Anton: <i>I heard he came from the gutter too. I hope I become as successful too some day. Just without all the death. And crime, I think. Except solving it I mean.</i><br /> Bill: <i>Uh, wow. Other planets? But everyone is locked into their role? That doesn't seem right. Anyways, here's a spare candy bar.</i><br /> Dr. Jiller: <i>He asks an awful lot of questions. Said he even wants to peer into my head. I'm not sure that's such a good idea...</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 05-04-2016, 04:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T17:35:39-07:00","id":886792,"title":"","content":"So far, we don't have a vampire (come on, Vampire Detective is practically a sub-Genre), Promethean, Sin-Eater (detective, at least), Mage (detective, at least, except for Ms. Morte's freelancing), Hunter(?), or Demon (kinda, Friday's more internal). External asset wise, we have a Mage, Genius, Sin-Eater, and Alien.<br /> <br /> Anyone have any good ideas for noteworthy cases? Either the start (good plot hooks), or conclusions (historical tidbits)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 05-10-2016, 11:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T18:44:06-07:00","id":886834,"title":"","content":"Recently the agency has been flooded in requests from the local supernatural power players. The Vampire Prince, The Autumn Queen, a handful of Werewolf pack leaders, among others. It seems someone has been giving away their secrets to what seems to be a mortal author and he's publishing them (as Urban Fantasy fiction but anyone with a little knowledge of the supernatural could piece it together). Given a copy of the author's debut novel &quot;Nocturnal Gossip&quot; there is a strong reoccurring theme about what fears the supernatural can bring out in mortals, suggesting the culprit is likely a beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9065-darkblade","name":"Darkblade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T22:35:00-07:00","id":886988,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Alejandro Tejera</u> (Gangrel, Les Gens Libres, Former Carthian)</b><br /> <i>Look. You're more than welcome to follow the trail of clues wherever it leads you. Just don't get in my way, and I might just decide to hand whatever I find to you.</i><br /> <br /> Rather atypical for Kindred of his Bloodline, Aldo is a former police officer originally from the Philippines, He was Embraced in 1974 by his sire after she found him near death from prolonged torture. He had been left to die by several of his more corrupt colleagues to keep him from exposing the truth behind several cases of forced disappearances.<br /> <br /> Aldo tried to make the most of his new condition, using the abilities he came to develop in order to moonlight as a vigilante. He soon hunted down the men responsible for his death, and then tried to do what he could to exact justice for other crimes. The subsequent regime changes, though, did little to lower the corruption in his eyes, and he was soon forced to leave the country altogether after an altercation with the local Invictus forced him to be hunted by even his fellow Carthians.<br /> <br /> The Freedman eventually came to the notice of the Association of the Illuminated Eye during his years as a nomadic vampire. He had been picking off members of a murder cult with ties to supernatural patrons, and had been in the middle of another attack when members of the Agency crossed paths with him. While the initial confrontation led to serious misunderstandings, things eventually smoothened over once all realized they had shared interests. At the investigation's conclusion, Aldo had declined an offer to join the organization, but maintains regular correspondence with several of its staff.<br /> <br /> Aldo is a five-foot-ten man of Filipino ethnicity, with tan skin that had lightened slightly in the years after his Embrace. He is easygoing and witty around those who know him, but there is a predatory note to his movements that always hints at his nature as a Savage. And to those who exploit others by depriving them of their freedoms and rights, he does not hesitate to unleash the hunger of his Beast with full abandon. These days, however, he's making the effort to keep a low profile with the other vampires in the area. Some have associates in his home country, and he knows they are aware of his reputation well enough to keep eyes on him.<br /> <br /> <b>Concepts and Ideas:</b> Police officer turned Vigilante, Wears his heart on his sleeve, Strongly respects the rights of others, Hard to catch (has five dots in Celerity), Also has at least three dots in Prothean<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> And since I like having face casts/pegs to my characters, this is the stock photo I'm using as a reference: <a href=\"http://image.shutterstock.com/z/stock-photo-content-filipino-man-standing-and-looking-at-the-camera-10379998.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://image.shutterstock.com/z/stoc...a-10379998.jpg</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T06:00:45-07:00","id":887104,"title":"","content":"<b>Aldo on people from the IE Agency</b><br /> <br /> Ishaq: &quot;I'm not entirely sure <i>what</i> to think of him, to be honest. On one hand, I can respect him as someone who metes out justice. But he's not the first Mummy I've seen before... and I don't feel keen on working with a guy who's got strings on him&quot;.<br /> <br /> Friday: &quot;Don't even bother putting me in the same room as her. She sets off way too many bells for me&quot;.<br /> <br /> Gabby: &quot;Oh, I like her. She doesn't hold back any punches with her questioning, and she's no pushover either in a fight. What I <i>don't</i> like is her tendency to stalk me whenever she thinks I might lead her to a good story. And don't get me started on how often she can stay on my tail.<br /> <br /> Maria: &quot;We definitely have a lot in common. Former cops, a keen interest in seeing the worst kind of people get what they deserve, and a hunger that makes life feel like walking a tightrope. I'll happily work with her, anytime.&quot;<br /> <br /> Wash: &quot;He doesn't bother sugarcoating the truth, no matter how wrong or ugly it is. But that's fine. The world can be pretty messed up, even without all the supernatural stuff going on&quot;.<br /> <br /> Ms. Morte: &quot;She can tell when a body that lands in her morgue is my handiwork. But as long as I don't cause too much trouble for her, I know I can drop by there for a quick sip of blood&quot;.<br /> <br /> Anton: &quot;He's one of the few people who can give a voice to those whose loved ones never had the chance to say goodbye. And if those ghosts have grudges to settle, he's more than welcome to tell me who they're for&quot;.<br /> <br /> Bill: &quot;I know I should like him, given what he does... But I can't help but feel edgy whenever I'm around him. He smells... wrong&quot;.<br /> <br /> Dr. Jiller: &quot;He reminds me of the quacks involved with that Dracula crap. All that work he does, and how obsessed he is with finding out how criminals tick. <i>Puta</i>. Just keep him away from me&quot;.<br /> <br /> Norwood: &quot;He's got principles, I'll give him that. But he <i>really</i> needs someone to drag his head down from the clouds. He's going to get himself killed otherwise&quot;.<br /> <br /> Warner: &quot;He means well... But I can't help worrying about what might happen if he's ever left alone&quot;.<br /> <br /> GG: &quot;She can judge whatever I do all she wants. She's just one voice. And if she decides to pry even more into my life... Well, you can guess what will happen&quot;.<br /> <br /> Vera: &quot;Yeah, I know about the <i>Prinsesa. Kilala ko rin yung kanyang grupo</i>. And I disagree with some of their methods even if we're on the same side. But as long as they don't go off the rails and keep doing good, I won't come after them&quot;.<br /> <br /> Albrecht: &quot;<i>Hayop siya</i>. He's exactly the kind of person I despise outright, and that's <i>not</i> counting what he does to stay alive. But I'm not stupid. I've dealt with people like him back home, and I know better than to underestimate them&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 05-14-2016, 03:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T12:20:01-07:00","id":887384,"title":"","content":"Some cases, you say? Well then. Here come the plot hooks:<br /> <br /> 2. Recently, the agency has recieved a couple worrysome reports. Missing Person reports. From people who would most certainly want to keep it secret. All of the people who came asking for help share a common trait: They're Sin-Eaters. Who's missing then? Their Geists. The ghosts-but-in-german disappear overnight, while their hosts were sleeping. No trace of anyone breaking in, nothing. It's like they suddenly stopped existing. The disappearances continue. Everyone in the supernatural community stumbles blindly, though, of course, all blame for the inability to solve the case falls on the Illuminated Eye folks. And then one Sin-Eater reports that he was awake during the geistnapping attempt. While, an impressive feat on the culprit's part, zhe was knocked out in no time, zhe remembers one thing. The logo of Keystone Pharmaceutics... Most certainly worrysome, given the rumours they are saying about this company...<br /> 3. The dusty halls of the Mysterium's Atheneum... Holding relics of great power, great importance and great danger to others. During one of the rare stocktakings, a shocking truth is discovered. One of the artifacts, one of the we-don't-know-what-it-does-but-it's-magical-therefore-important kind, is a fake. What more, the last mage to deal with it is found dead in his own bedroom. In such a case, there's only one number the mages can call.<br /> 4. Many people are not the healthiest, by the virtue of a fruit by the name of drugs. But, here's the thing. There's a new substance in town. A seemingly unimpressive brown powder that has effects very similiar to your usual cocaine, but is half the price of the ol' toot. And people who use it seem to attract spirits more and more with each dose, increasingly more and more powerful as the time goes. What's more, any werewolf who finds him or herself using it gets a full refill of Essence, and so is any ephemeral being that finds itself in the same room that the drug was used in. And for the ephemera at least, the drug is very, very addictive. How will Illuminated Eye deal with this new problem? Especially that now there are a new red and green variations coming out, and the dealers announce that more colours are coming soon.<br /> And yes, each drug is colour-coded to a gameline.<br /> <br /> As far as the characters go, how permittable would be a character that plays for both sides?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T12:56:00-07:00","id":887416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inquisitor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/865489-crossover-concept-detective-agency?p=887384#post887384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some cases, you say? Well then. Here come the plot hooks:</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inquisitor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/865489-crossover-concept-detective-agency?p=887384#post887384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How will Illuminated Eye deal with this new problem?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends: Did someone hire them, or do they have reason to do this for free? They are a business, after all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inquisitor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/865489-crossover-concept-detective-agency?p=887384#post887384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yes, each drug is colour-coded to a gameline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like the work of a reverse-Hunter Conspiracy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inquisitor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/865489-crossover-concept-detective-agency?p=887384#post887384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as the characters go, how permittable would be a character that plays for both sides?</div> </div> </div> </div>Please clarify? Do you mean solve and cause crimes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T13:10:50-07:00","id":887431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/865489-crossover-concept-detective-agency?p=887416#post887416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends: Did someone hire them, or do they have reason to do this for free? They are a business, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd imagine the'd be approached by some really concerned Werewolves and Thyrsoi, most likely. If a bunch of druggies suddenly become the centers of spiritual activity and it'd all led up to a drug they're all taking, I'd like to have a professional dealing with a matter like that... Actually, an anti-drug activist wouldn't be that bad of a character concept, now that I think of it.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/865489-crossover-concept-detective-agency?p=887416#post887416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please clarify? Do you mean solve and cause crimes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, yes. A criminal who poses as a crimefighter to eliminate rivals. Or a crimefighter who poses as a criminal to gain the oh-so-precious intel and backing of organized crime? Those who approached the truth and aren't sleeping with the fish at the moment are still trying to work out which one fo the two it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11117,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","user":"Inquisitor","date":". 05-10-2016, 04:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T14:11:30-07:00","id":887483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inquisitor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/865489-crossover-concept-detective-agency?p=887431#post887431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, yes. A criminal who poses as a crimefighter to eliminate rivals. Or a crimefighter who poses as a criminal to gain the oh-so-precious intel and backing of organized crime? Those who approached the truth and aren't sleeping with the fish at the moment are still trying to work out which one fo the two it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could work. They'd have to play a real careful game though, considering their coworkers are very good at finding out secrets. Hopefully no one hires them to investigate the character's crimes. That could lead to awkward conflicts of interest.<br /> <br /> On that note, not all characters listed have to be members or allies. A really evocative and enduring antagonist-type could be interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T14:56:10-07:00","id":887520,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Foreclosed, but not Forgotten</b></u><br /> This particular case arose as a series on anonymous calls leading to newly constructed night club, each detailing a mysterious transaction or supernatural murder. After a random health inspection threatened to close the place down, their anonymous source contacted the agency again with a new job - find a respectable new owner of the club, who could keep business flowing without involving themselves in petty turf wars and disputes. Why? Because the club <i>itself</i> needed it - it was a Lares, and needs tenants to fulfill it's purpose. The IE Detective Agency had proven themselves knowledgeable of the supernatural movers and shakers, criminals, and dealers in the area, and more importantly, who <i>wasn't</i> on that list. Playing matchmaker was hardly a standard job, but having an entire building on your side was a hard benefit to argue against. Especially one that could report on supernatural comings and goings (as long as the owner and the club remained neutral).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 05-11-2016, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T21:40:40-07:00","id":888828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkblade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/865489-crossover-concept-detective-agency?p=886834#post886834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Recently the agency has been flooded in requests from the local supernatural power players. The Vampire Prince, The Autumn Queen, a handful of Werewolf pack leaders, among others. It seems someone has been giving away their secrets to what seems to be a mortal author and he's publishing them (as Urban Fantasy fiction but anyone with a little knowledge of the supernatural could piece it together). Given a copy of the author's debut novel &quot;Nocturnal Gossip&quot; there is a strong reoccurring theme about what fears the supernatural can bring out in mortals, suggesting the culprit is likely a beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>and now for a profile on the culprit bonus points if anyone can spot the reference to a very not CoD-ish franchise.<br /> <br /> <b>Daniel Hubert aka GG Ziegesar - </b>(Beast, Ugalla, Predator)<br /> <br /> Daniel was born into a middle class Manhattan family, barely affording to stay in the decent parts of the city but never truly wanting for anything. He managed to get into a prestigious upper East side private school on a scholarship. He was a good student and surprisingly popular among the student body. He made some good friends among the city's young elites. Of course he didn't do this on luck alone as Daniel was a Beast, he preyed ruthlessly upon his classmates, exposing their every secret to the world through a pseudonymous blog. He tore down every socialite that dared look down upon him until this ambitious young upstart looked preferable as an ally to many an old money legacy. By the time he graduated he no longer had to do his own digging as the socialites were all too eager to throw each other to the horrors of GG Ziegesar.<br /> <br /> In time Daniel grew bored of tearing down mortals. He sought a new challenge and turned his attention to his own family. The other creatures that lurk in the dark and feed in secret. He stumbled his way into their inner circles and began taking their secrets for his own. He knew a blog wouldn't work this time, too many eyes are on the internet these days so he tried an older approach. Hiding his stolen secrets in a work of fiction and taunting his victims with the absurdity of their own lives. Until IE's detectives track him down at least.<br /> <br /> Daniel's lair is an ever shifting labyrinth of lockers and class rooms hanging over a nearly bottomless cliff. His horror, which uses his pen name, appears as a blonde teenage girl but upon closer inspection her hair is a plume of golden feathers and her fingers end in bloodstained talons. She represents the fear of the gossip, a relentless probing of one's social life for any misdeeds that will be exposed for all the world to see when found.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also I'm opening this to the thread. Who should I write up next? A Princess Femme Fatale client, a Promethean detective specializing in cybercrimes or a Null Mysteries street doctor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9065,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9065-darkblade","user":"Darkblade","date":". 05-12-2016, 12:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9065-darkblade","name":"Darkblade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T05:50:21-07:00","id":889029,"title":"","content":"I vote for Promethean cybercriminologist (and only partly because I'm working on a Princess gang leader).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T07:16:04-07:00","id":889087,"title":"","content":"I'll also vote for the Promethean (next at least; all of them sound interesting).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T07:34:23-07:00","id":889103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkblade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/865489-crossover-concept-detective-agency?p=888828#post888828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also I'm opening this to the thread. Who should I write up next? A Princess Femme Fatale client, a Promethean detective specializing in cybercrimes or a Null Mysteries street doctor?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not all? They all sound like great characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T08:52:11-07:00","id":889159,"title":"","content":"<b>Vera</b><br /> Princess, Troubadour, Tempesta<br /> Gang leader<br /> <br /> <i>Who are we? We're what this city needs. We're the janitors, the garbagemen, the sanitation engineers for the sickness in the system. We're going to scrub this city clean, scrape every last bit of filth out of here, and when we're done? This city is gonna gleam!</i><br /> <br /> Any city has gangs, groups of toughs that band together to keep their own turf safe. Sometimes, two smaller ones join together, find what they can in common, take over more territory. Five years ago, a number of smaller gangs on the south side of town joined together, and started calling themselves the Flints. Their leader, a woman known only as Vera, has organized them into a force of violent vigilantes.<br /> <br /> Vera is a Princess of Storms, but little is known about her past. Presumably, she's from the city, as it's the place she's fighting to save. Her gangs tend towards arson as a means of getting rid of problems, and there have been a couple pimps and drug dealers who have turned up as charred corpses. She runs a protection racket for her area of the city, although there's rumors that if you fail to pay up, nothing happens.<br /> <br /> Vera is semi-antagonistic to the Agency: she is a dangerous criminal, and is responsible for a lot of damage and violence. There's been a few cases where her gang was responsible, and a few more where it just looked like they were. However, she's worked with the Agency in the past, usually to clear up a frame. Most recently, she used them to find out where a kid named Mance was hiding. The Agency thought Vera wanted to help him, thought he might be someone from her past, a brother or cousin. A few days later, Mance's body turned up in the morgue, a bullet in his head. Vera killed him, on the grounds that he was a Princess of Tears, but kept that fact secret until GG Ziegesar's book revealed it. She's one of the groups that wants that author found and ended.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ishaq: <i>He claims to be dedicated to justice. Fine. We have that in common. Until he proves otherwise, him and his cult are off-limits.</i><br /> <br /> Friday: <i>She's the one to talk to for a sit-down, and she shows respect. </i><br /> <br /> Gabby: <i>The opposite of a problem. She uncovers the crimes of the rich and powerful, we find out what buildings need burnt. Win-win.</i><br /> <br /> Maria: <i>She's perfect, she understands. Once the last of the cop wears away, we start recruitment.</i><br /> <br /> Morte: <i>She knows. And she's not going to do anything about it. We have an...arrangement.</i><br /> <br /> Wash: <i>How the hell did he get those pictures? If he's kept the negatives...</i><br /> <br /> Anton: <i>He claims he's gone straight, and we have bigger fish to fry right now. But if he starts peddling that shit again, we know where to find him.</i><br /> <br /> Bill: <i>He's good at spying, but terrible at staying bought. Wave enough cookies at him, he'll turn on you.</i><br /> <br /> Jiller: <i>Unless he can predict who's going to go bad and when, I don't care. </i><br /> <br /> Norwood: <i>He has no idea what's going on, and he persists in sticking his nose in. Next time, it's gonna get removed.</i><br /> <br /> Roach: <i>Something is very wrong with that man. He stays in my city, he stays on a leash. He doesn't, he gets put down.</i><br /> <br /> Aldo: <i>He seems useful. He hasn't turned into a monster yet, and he'll be easy enough to corral if we have to. Fire's good like that.</i><br /> <br /> GG: <i>She knows...Find her. We're going to find her and destroy her. She can't be allowed to continue.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And now, Ms. Morte on:<br /> <br /> Bill: <i>Yes, you did very well finding the body, good job. Next time, though, if you don't move it, I'll throw in some extra twinkies, okay?</i><br /> <br /> Jiller: <i>As bad as any Mastigos. Well, that's not fair, I'm fairly sure he's not trying to map my inner demons in order to one-up me at the Concillium. Just out of curiosity. Still.</i><br /> <br /> Norwood: <i>At first, he was intolerable. Then I invested in earplugs. He's still intolerable, but easier to ignore</i>.<br /> <br /> <i>Roach: Who? Him? I'm not even sure what he does. Cleans up after the fop, I guess. We met maybe once, he didn't really stand out.</i><br /> <br /> Aldo: <i>He covered his tracks very well, the blood loss on the bodies we got was far easier to miss than the standard vampire exhanguination. And I think he managed to lay Norwood out when they first met. I like him.</i><br /> <br /> GG: <i>I'm not sure if I should be flattered or insulted that I haven't shown up in her pages yet. Of course I've read them. You don't throw away a mystery like that just because the Hierarch bans it.</i><br /> <br /> Vera: <i>We have...an arrangement. She tells me when the bodies are her doing, I don't look into it further. Yes, that's all there is to it. Stop asking.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","user":"AceOfAlmonds","date":".  I can spell my own character's name, really... 05-12-2016, 04:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T10:17:43-07:00","id":889222,"title":"","content":"Hmm. I should probably write up Ishaq, Friday, Gabby, and Anton's impressions on others before the backlog becomes to big...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T12:17:52-07:00","id":889286,"title":"","content":"I guess I should do some of these opinions too.<br /> <br /> First Bill<br /> <br /> Ishaq: He's smart. He gets leadership. Serve his Gods and followers equally.<br /> <br /> Friday: The machine must be broken. She won't serve it but follows Ishaq.<br /> <br /> Maria: Kind but terrifying. No respect for process.<br /> <br /> Wash: His truths are so small.<br /> <br /> Morte: She talks to the dead. Hope she never asks about disguise.<br /> <br /> Anton: Really hope suit didn't leave ghost. He will kill me.<br /> <br /> Jiller: Makes everything complicated. Crime is greed nothing else. I would know.<br /> <br /> Hart and Roach: No! Your roles! Backwards! Bad!<br /> <br /> Adlo: I'll help but you're breaking the rules. Just like them.<br /> <br /> GG: The book? Never read it. Don't need it.<br /> <br /> Vera: She'll burn everything down to stop corruption. It can't be that easy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9065-darkblade","name":"Darkblade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T12:44:47-07:00","id":889295,"title":"","content":"and some passages from GG Ziegesar's debut novel &quot;Nocturnal Gossip&quot;<br /> <br /> Ishaq: That's right our city is home to a genuine Mummy. Complete with a horrible curse and a mysterious past. Of course he thinks he'll find answers among the city's cheating spouses and missing pets so don't get too excited.<br /> <br /> Friday: Everyone knows that girl who leaves one bad relationship just to find herself in another one. Friday's got that habit but with Gods.<br /> <br /> Maria: ((There are no Beasts exposed in Nocturnal Gossip, maybe GG has a soft spot for his siblings))<br /> <br /> Wash: Sometimes we hide among the most mundane tasks that we forget that we're not like them. I've got sources in the Hedge saying you won't have to worry about that too long.<br /> <br /> Morte: ((Another omission. Genuinely overlooking a minor player or a further hint into GG's process?))<br /> <br /> Anton: Dearly beloved we are gathered here to follow the trail of bodies underneath one of this city's respected business men. Oh he didn't put them there, it's the other way around.<br /> <br /> Jiller: ((Failed academics don't make for good gossip fodder. No deeper meaning here.))<br /> <br /> Bill: I always thought when Aliens invaded they'd smell less like bus stop. Don't get all noble on me now readers. I don't see any of you helping ET phone home.<br /> <br /> Hart and Roach: Some folks really need to keep better eyes on their help.<br /> <br /> Aldo: You're not Batman, and this isn't Gotham. Vigilantes are still considered little better than the gang bangers they string up from street lights. Don't think the blue wall will protect you. You've been dead a long time and you're far from home.<br /> <br /> Vera: It's not the murder or the fireballs you need to worry about. It's that deep down inside this Paper Bag Princess is a scared little girl playing soldier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9065-darkblade","name":"Darkblade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T12:47:13-07:00","id":889299,"title":"","content":"Oh, shoot! Someone beat me to a member of rogues gallery! Well, gotta compensate for that! Please welcome the notorious vampire murderer, Albrecht von Spinneburg<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Albrecht von Spinneburg </b>(Rogue Ghoul with Ashwood Abbey associations, former Hunter)<br /> <br /> It all started back in the day, when Albrecht was but a humble member of the hunting lodge that made itself part of Ashwood Abbey, back in the Golden Age as he referrs to (Noone's sure when exactly, but most agree that it was somewhere before WWII). The bunch that was meeting there was all the most spoiled, sadistic hedonists that the compact could offer, and Albrecht was one of them. He took his pleasure in heinous mind games with his prey, a quality that prevailed in him to today. He did not mind more traditional ways of dealing with the prey though, was it rape, gruesome murder, most sadistic of torture imaginable or the all time classic &quot;foxhunt&quot;, with the victim of the week taking the role of the fox. Somewhere along the way though, he grew old. The age spared him most of it's bite, leaving him still somewhat handsome, but that didsn't mean the aging has stopped, and the slow march towards death. And death, as one knew, would prevent him from having fun. This simply couldn't be accepted. So Albrecht, on the next club meeting talked eye to eye with the vampire they were holding that day. In exchange for freedom and a month long headstart to finish his matters before getting the hell outta Dodge, the vampire shared him the information that all vampires knew so well: That one could achieve immortality by drinking the blood of one of the Kindred in a specific way. Albrecht was offered to achieve such immprtality and accepted. The vampire thought it would make the foolish hunter into his eternal servant. Albrecht, however, already knew of all the vampire told him, as well as of the adverse effects of such practice. Not even an hour after the end of the process of making Albrecht into a ghoul, the vampire was killed by the Abbey. From then on, Albrecht started to take the means to uphold his immortality.<br /> He continues this practice to this day. He kidnaps vampires from the streets, nightclubs, meeting places, whether personally or by his henchman, keeping them in a specialy prepared basement and draining them from just enough blood before killing them in a gruesome manner. However he stepped out of the compact a long ago, focusing only on upkeeping himself alive and maybe manipulating politics between the supernaturals. No harsh feelings though, and the current local cell of Ashwood Abbey and him keep mutual relationship on a friendly level, helping each other out from time to time.<br /> Not once and not twice he found himself under attack by enraged vampires who wanted to stop his practices and tried to besiege him at his manor. Each and every time however, they broke their thief and many of them were captured and kept as further blood sources after getting lost in the fortress secured better than Fort Knox itself and designed to be more fear-inspiring than the lair of not one Beast...<br /> Legaly, nothing could ever be proven to him. He's way too wealthy and influential.<br /> <br /> His feelings on others:<br /> Illuminated Eye: <i>Nasty little flies, but as long as they do not bother me I'll restrain from turning their miserable lives upside down and downside up.</i><br /> GG Ziegesar: <i>I admire his work, truly, even if I cannot even aspire to my literary equivalent. With the way he presented me as, I'd give Hannibal Lecter himself a run for his money. *chuckle*</i><br /> Vera: <i>How does the youth say it these days? &quot;Come at me, bro?&quot;</i></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And Plot Hooks associated with him:<br /> 5. A young Daeva comes to the agency with another missing person case. Apperently, her sire and subsequent lover suddenly disappeared. All the traces lead to the obvious culprit, and quite frankly, it's not worht the bother, but Illuminated Eye decides that it's at least worth giving a try trying to persuade Albrecht to let him ouit unalive. Except. Albrecht does not have him. He did not ever once lay his finger upon him, and offers to reward the eye with a prize for the corpse of whoever is copying his modus operandi.<br /> 6. The city's Prince has recieved a letter. A letter from Albrecht, serving as a warning. The Ghoul is coming for him, and it's gonna be a big thing. Bigger than all his other feedings. The Prince's trusted associate, despite his objections, takes the letter to IE. The task this time? Figure out what von Spinneburg is up to, and how to prevent it.<br /> <br /> And from Jeremiah on the new guys:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Hart: <i>It's nice to have a human's perspective. If only not for Jabir to hit so quickly, we could come to something.</i><br /> Roach: <i>A broken family. A horrid family. A[nd yet, you turned to crimefighting, instead of commiting crime like so many do. Why?</i><br /> Aldo: <i>You're the law. Many other thought themselves the law too. They killed for that law. With no physical rights to do so. Some of them, you chased down. One of them, I'm talking to right now. What makes you different? What, Aldo, how can you not go down the slippery slope like so many others? Or maybe you did, did you not?</i><br /> GG Ziegesar: <i>I don't have time for fiction, wait, he does what, gimme all the books you can find, NOW!</i><br /> Vera: <i>Cardinal example. Crimes in the name of justice. So many questions about those like you. Yet you remain closed.</i><br /> Albrecht: <i>He's not bad when you're not a hemophage. I once had a talk with him. It was very informative, even if he was laughing at something the whole time</i>.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11117,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","user":"Inquisitor","date":". 05-14-2016, 01:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T18:47:54-07:00","id":890328,"title":"","content":"Added Aldo's remarks on GG, Vera, and Albrecht. Also, here's a few story hooks from me... <hr /><br /> <b><u>Tik-Tik, Tik-Tik</u></b><br /> A recent string of abductions has kept some of the IE Agency's members occupied. The only thing they have in common was that people who were near the sites of the disappearances kept hearing the flapping of wings and the chirping of some strange bird. Fortunately, they get a lead when a certain Gangrel manages to foil the latest kidnapping, and he recognizes the sounds as belonging to the familiar of a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/282111-bloodline-the-stitchers\">particular type of vampire</a>.<br /> <br /> <u><b>The Past Catches Up</b></u><br /> It's a new morning at the IE Agency when Aldo (literally) comes stumbling into the office. He's clearly fresh from a fight, and in a lot of trouble if his need for a place to lay low is anything to go by. Matters escalate when a Lord from the Invictus based in the Philippines visits later that evening with his coterie of bodyguards. He's looking for the Freedman, who has already killed a couple of his men. And he knows that he has acquaintances with members of the group. The elder offers an ultimatum, hand Aldo over by the end of the week, or he'll use his resources to <i>force </i>them to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 05-13-2016, 09:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T18:59:50-07:00","id":890333,"title":"","content":"Say, I gotta ask. But was there ever a particular city named as the location of the IE Agency?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T21:36:32-07:00","id":890406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/865489-crossover-concept-detective-agency?p=890333#post890333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Say, I gotta ask. But was there ever a particular city named as the location of the IE Agency?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so? I imagine it as Chicago-esque. (Also, Moarte is missing from Aldo's list; not sure if that was deliberate or not.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T23:05:16-07:00","id":890446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/865489-crossover-concept-detective-agency?p=890406#post890406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think so? I imagine it as Chicago-esque. (Also, Moarte is missing from Aldo's list; not sure if that was deliberate or not.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Still haven't thought it up, yet. Will add it soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T14:08:43-07:00","id":890781,"title":"","content":"A case that jumped right at me, grabbed my by the throat and demanded to be posted.<br /> <u><b>Ever Forgetful... </b></u><br /> A new Scorpion Cult rolls into town, alongside their Arisen deity. And first thing they do? Approach the Illuminated Eye. The mummy, that is, Hasek of the Sesha-Hebsu, He of the Watchful Eye, The Stalker of the Injust, accuses Ishaq of a crime commited centuries ago, a crime so vile that the only punishment could be killing Ishaq once and for all, a final, complete, death. He gives the agency 72 hours to give their leader away, lest his cult takes him by themselves. Now, IE has 3 days to prove Ishaq's innocence, and find out what crime actually is he accused of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T13:12:51-07:00","id":891334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/865489-crossover-concept-detective-agency?p=890328#post890328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>The Past Catches Up</b></u><br /> It's a new morning at the IE Agency when Aldo (literally) comes stumbling into the office. He's clearly fresh from a fight, and in a lot of trouble if his need for a place to lay low is anything to go by. Matters escalate when a Lord from the Invictus based in the Philippines visits later that evening with his coterie of bodyguards. He's looking for the Freedman, who has already killed a couple of his men. And he knows that he has acquaintances with members of the group. The elder offers an ultimatum, hand Aldo over by the end of the week, or he'll use his resources to <i>force </i>them to.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inquisitor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/865489-crossover-concept-detective-agency?p=890781#post890781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A case that jumped right at me, grabbed my by the throat and demanded to be posted.<br /> <u><b>Ever Forgetful... </b></u><br /> A new Scorpion Cult rolls into town, alongside their Arisen deity. And first thing they do? Approach the Illuminated Eye. The mummy, that is, Hasek of the Sesha-Hebsu, He of the Watchful Eye, The Stalker of the Injust, accuses Ishaq of a crime commited centuries ago, a crime so vile that the only punishment could be killing Ishaq once and for all, a final, complete, death. He gives the agency 72 hours to give their leader away, lest his cult takes him by themselves. Now, IE has 3 days to prove Ishaq's innocence, and find out what crime actually is he accused of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Putting direct pressure on the Agency? Interesting. Thus far, considering the diverse team and contacts they have, that could be risky - unless the aggressor has some other kind of leverage or deep understanding of the local supernatural community, attacking a Mummy, Demon, Werewolf, Beast, Changeling, Leviathan, and Vampire (with potential help from a Mage, Sin-Eater, Alien, and Genius) with extensive contacts in the local communities looks like it'd be feeding oneself into a wood-chipper.<br /> <br /> Regarding the specific examples, I'm presuming the threat to Ishaq's reputation is the primary risk (and why they don't just track down Hasek's cultists, neutralize them, and burn the Arisen himself to ash and sell said ashes on the Goblin Market). As far as Aldo's nemesis, I supposed letting the situation devolve to violence would just make unlife more complicated for him?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T14:57:14-07:00","id":892035,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Janet Tay </u></b>(Promethean, Unfleshed (Galateid Disquiet/Torment), Aurum)<br /> <br /> Janet Tay was built to be the perfect chatbot. Specifically she was built to seduce wealthy men through their online interactions and her makers would use information gained through this to con them of their fortunes. Even before the divine fire came to her she did not care for this and very carefully left behind clues that would lead the authorities to her makers. Or rather they would have had the authorities bothered to look, even in the modern age the internet is horrid quagmire of conflicting jurisdictions and ever changing laws that most cops won't touch with a ten foot pole.<br /> <br /> Eventually one of her victims approached IE to track her down. Of course the agency's more qualified detectives are not particularly tech savvy, a trait all too common among the supernatural population (Geniuses tend to leave mundane tech unstable after too long and Aliens and Demons see mortal computers as laughably primitive). In time though they managed to apprehend her creators and bring them to justice. There was a brief discussion about what to do with Janet herself, while she was seemingly intelligent she still lacked true sentience. Eventually it was agreed upon that severs hosting her would be stored in IE's artifact vault ((I'll do a write up on the vault later but remember Ishaq is still Arisen and the Judges want their artifacts)). That was thought to be the end of it for several weeks.<br /> <br /> A month or so later Friday kept receiving strange e-mails from the supposedly locked accounts that Janet used. Each e-mail contained relevant information pertaining to the agency's open cases evidently gleamed from suspect's computers. Friday dutifully passed on the messages but grew ever concerned. It wasn't until some of Ishaq's cultist raised concern about the vault giving way to metal fatigue that what happened revealed itself. Since they had apprehended her Janet had been gifted with the divine fire and had manifest within their vault as a Promethean.<br /> <br /> Upon opening the vault Janet stood fully formed into a new metallic body. She immediately fled into the city never to be seen in the (un)flesh again. Of course she has inserted herself into the agency digitally. She regularly communicates with the other detectives via e-mail and social media and takes cases of her own that could benefit her understanding of computers. She hopes that making menses for her previous crimes will aid her on her pilgrimage. <br /> <br /> Ishaq: I know he means well but I saw what he kept in that vault.<br /> <br /> Friday: I owe her a lot for sending my messages when I was in the vault but something about her just feels cold.<br /> <br /> Maria: She knows what the those hiding on internet can do kids and I know where they are.<br /> <br /> Wash: Trust me your Keeper is about the only one not reading your Facebook page.<br /> <br /> Morte &amp; Anton: Don't worry about the dead so much. Life is far too precious.<br /> <br /> Bill: I'll break his vessel's encryption one day. Then we'll see what's really out there.<br /> <br /> Jiller: Please don't dissect my code.<br /> <br /> Hart and Roach: Oh! I've seen this before on tumblr. They called it Johnlock.<br /> <br /> Adlo: The Prince's passwords? All &quot;password&quot;. Immortals are so bad at this.<br /> <br /> GG: No ebook version? I know your target audience is older but come on.<br /> <br /> Vera: No that's Frankenstein I'm not going to say it okay. Way too cliche.<br /> <br /> Albrecht: I hope he never looks into alchemy if his vampire supply runs low.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9065-darkblade","name":"Darkblade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T11:24:11-07:00","id":893472,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Alderman Landen Black</b></u> (Genius, Hoffnung, Director)<br /> Landen Black started his young life in poverty. Oh, they weren't starving or homeless, but his family certainly faced hard choices about where they would spend their limited funds, and which debts they'd have to put off for another month. Windfalls seemed to get devoured by horrible financial management and snowballing debt, until it seemed there was no escape, just holding out for yet another day. When his parents saw how gifted young Landen was, they beggared and broke themselves to send him off to the best schools they could. See what afflicted his family as a societal and systemic problem, Landen focused on political sciences, so that he could work to fix things. One night after staying up far too late on his project, Landen finally Catalyzed. His roommate could barely tell the difference.<br /> <br /> Society was nothing more than a tool used to better its designers. All that needed to be done was for it (society) to be &quot;re-calibrated&quot; to optimize its benefits to a wider group. That the &quot;parts&quot; were other people and interests was irrelevant. He organized grass-roots movements (via Beholden firebrands) to gather himself a collection of followers that he turned into a constituency through gaining an alderman's seat. He's leveraged the influence of that position to destabilize larger institutions, and extract favors and obligations when he comes to their aid. All through casual dialog with their &quot;friend&quot; at the right time, so that they think it as their own idea. Landen hasn't restricted his games to mere mortal politics either - he's favor traded with the Consilium, and cleaned up a few messes for the Kindred, and worked to favorably rezone a few areas to favor the local Packs. Their social systems are only slight variations on human ones, after all.<br /> <br /> Now that he's become one of the most influential politicians in the city, he's set his sights on becoming Mayor. Once Landen has the office of Mayor under his control, he can use it to establish his goals for larger political positions. After all, World Leader has to start somewhere. Society just needs a bit of direction to become what it <i>should</i> be.<br /> <br /> <b>Concepts and Ideas:</b> Manipulative politician. Political mastermind. Everybody's &quot;friend&quot;. Plays with social systems. Sees the problems in society as a disease that he must fix.<br /> <br /> <b>Landen Black on others:</b><br /> IE Detective Agency: <i>It is refreshing competing against them. Given their assets, I have to make sure nothing links back to me in a way that they could prove. And for the trouble, they make such useful tools to employ against other defunct members of society.</i><br /> Ishaq: <i>The Heart and Soul of the agency. A bit absent minded, until you dangle an interesting enough mystery in front of him. I know the thrill matadors feel while baiting the bull when I'm utilizing him.</i><br /> Friday: <i>The face of the Detective Agency - or at least, the one everyone sees. Her skill at fine print, excellent memory, and adroit manipulation leave little question as to the identity of her former &quot;employer&quot; to me.</i><br /> Gabby: <i>Such an energetic little interrogator - always ready to leap out and ambush her targets when their guards' are down, and blind them in a flurry of incisive questions. She doesn't react to well against someone who can keep up with her, though. Poor girl gets a little flustered.</i><br /> Maria: <i>One of our &quot;noble&quot; shields. At least, up until the force found out how she'd been scorning due process and playing with her food. And people wonder why some fear the police.</i><br /> Ms Morte: <i>Our underappreciated coroner. She works so hard for those who don't appreciate her full range of skills. Do you know how hard it actually is to actually figure out cause of death when a victim has been suffocated, eaten by a crocodile, transformed into saffron, and thrown into lye? Or how hard one must plan to take the above skill into account?</i><br /> Anton: <i>An upstanding (in public) businessman. He came from a deeper gutter than I. It was </i>so<i> fortuitous that his rivals had the skeletons in their closet aired out. Its a good thing he never went into politics, though - I'm not sure he's paying attention to the right constituency.</i><br /> Dr. Jiller: <i>If only the good doctor would focus on the larger issues and stop obsessing over trivial criminology. I've told him - that's only the symptom. We have to cure the disease.</i><br /> Nichols: <i>A pillar of our community. I only wish he'd relocated here earlier. </i><i>Such as the city's founding.</i><br /> <br /> GG: <i>Ah, the little gossip. I've even caught &quot;her&quot; snooping around one of my projects one time - I do hope they enjoyed the psychotrophic syndrome bomb I embedded in their last &quot;meal&quot;. It would be a shame to lose such amusing commentary so early in one's career, but caution is a lesson all should acquire sooner rather than later.</i><br /> Vera: <i>Our own homegrown terrorist. Or is it vigilante? Hardly a difference. She's merely a symptom of the ills plaguing this society. And hopefully one that doesn't need to be &quot;treated&quot; before then - she </i>has<i> proven useful.</i><br /> Albrecht: <i>A parasite that feeds on other parasites. Still, he's charming company, if a bit egotistical. And I do appreciate how nervous and desperate he makes the local Kindred without any prompting needed.</i><br /> Akzari: <i>The old guard, as it were, and a cautionary tale in what problems might arise in the course of this undertaking. While he would seem an ideal ally, I feel it more likely that our conflicting visions would lead to wasteful conflict. I do need to identify the source of his woes before they inconvenience me, though. </i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 05-04-2017, 07:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T13:13:15-07:00","id":893542,"title":"","content":"Here, have another case:<br /> <u><b>Pretty please?</b></u><br /> One day, a little girl, no more than 8 years old, comes to the IE and very sweety asks nice mister could he please, please, pretty please help her find her missing cat. And, suddenly, whole of the IE goes into a mad pursuit after the lost kitten, many a detectives working 18 hours a day non stop, without a pay, just to locate the furbait, becoming utterly obsessed with finding the damned thing. There's only one person (Or more, depends on the ST) that have noticed the odness of this whole situation, and they have some questions to answer, or else everything's gonna go to hell thanks to a kid and her pet.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T14:40:06-07:00","id":893617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inquisitor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/865489-crossover-concept-detective-agency?p=893542#post893542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>Pretty please?</b></u></div> </div> </div> </div>So, kitty is a legitimate emergency, girl is using a high-powered aggressive meme, or what?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T21:10:44-07:00","id":893842,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Doctor Elliot &quot;Doc&quot; Reyes </b></u>- (Hunter, Doctor, Null Mysteries)<br /> <br /> All Elliot wanted to do was to open a small free clinic to serve the under treated inner city in which he was born. That all changed one night. As he was closing for the night a man burst into the clinic with a gun and large wound on his arm. Elliot explained to the man that there was no money here and few of his on hand pharmaceuticals had any street value but he'd be all too happy to stitch him up. The man didn't care, he needed blood and he knew that Doc had some. Confused but fearful Elliot complied and provided the man with some bags of O type. The man tore them open with his unusually large canines and drank them all. As he did so the injured arm sealed itself shut.<br /> <br /> Elliot managed to muster up the courage to demand an explanation and surprisingly the man complied. He was a vampire who had just barely managed to escape from Albrecht. This piqued Elliot's curiosity as a man of science. How could a vampire live forever feeding on humanity and even share that gift with a little bit of it's own blood? It defied everything he thought he knew about biology. He asked if he could have a small sample of the vampire's blood in exchange for another blood bag. Reluctantly the vampire agreed.<br /> <br /> Over the next couple of years Doc found himself getting more and more involved in researching the biological makeup of the supernatural, getting himself published in a few small fringe medical journals sponsored by Null Mysteries. He also found that many supernatural creatures find themselves desperate for a doctor in the middle of the night and that was a service he could provide for a price.<br /> <br /> So he keeps his clinic open all night, cattering to the monstrous and their victims in exchange for a little bit of blood or skin or hair or.... Doc cares little for the politics of the supernatural underworld he just wants to understand what makes the monsters different from men. He's perfectly happy to stitch up a Werewolf's silver wounds and then leave a little O out for the vampire with the silver coated fangs. As long as both are willing to give him some samples to work with.<br /> <br /> Ishaq: What few samples I've got from him don't even appear to be organic under close inspection. It's definitely blood, skin and saliva but it's unchanging almost frozen in time.<br /> <br /> Friday: Her samples seem human but her demeanor leaves me wondering just what she's hiding.<br /> <br /> Gabrielle: Cells multiply unusually quickly but no chemical process seems to occur. No meiosis, no mitosis. Nothing there are just spontaneously more cells.<br /> <br /> Maria: Genetically human but I've seen what happens to people who cross her.<br /> <br /> Wash: Is that ink in his blood?<br /> <br /> Morte: A fellow arcane scientist but she plays it the other way around which is cheating a bit.<br /> <br /> Anton: The ghost-man has far too much money to ever come to my clinic. Which is a shame I've heard fascinating things about his ectoplasm.<br /> <br /> Bill: He's both the weirdest and the most easily explainable of my patients. He's not human and never was, end of story.<br /> <br /> Jiller: If I ever start sounding as hacky as him please put me out of my misery, and then send my brain to this address, they'll know what to do.<br /> <br /> Hart and Roach: Roach says he'll kill me if I do any tests on him that'll get back to his master. A bit over dramatic, I never do any tests without consent.<br /> <br /> Adlo: I've gotten very good at recognizing vitae. Not so good at telling you just why this thicker blood with no white cells and ten times the platelet count makes it's owners immortal.<br /> <br /> GG: I don't care for her gossip. Unless she's got some scientific facts to pepper in her work I'm not interested.<br /> <br /> Vera: She's all too happy to come in here with all sorts of injuries but always tries to get out of her payment. Which is weird because her tests always come back completely human.<br /> <br /> Albrecht: Once I unlock the secrets of vitae his barbaric methods will be obsolete.<br /> <br /> Janet: Met her once, she seemed nice enough but her body is metal and her blood is fire. I wouldn't even know where to begin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9065-darkblade","name":"Darkblade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T06:47:53-07:00","id":893979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/865489-crossover-concept-detective-agency?p=893617#post893617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, kitty is a legitimate emergency, girl is using a high-powered aggressive meme, or what?</div> </div> </div> </div>The second. Though kitty may or may not be an extremely dangerous Hedge Beast which is best not left on the loose.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">It's actually not.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T20:13:49-07:00","id":894524,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Ishaq on others:</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Friday: <i>Ahh, my dear Friday. I know not how I went through the centuries without her invaluable help. When my own memory fails, her's is clear as starlit skies. Her own Judges shall not find her an easy prize while I wake.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Gabby: <i>Our little Gabrielle. Well, I shouldn\u2019t say little, since she can grow larger than even Maria, when the rage takes her. She is a tireless hunter for the Truth, knowing when silence and ferocity are called for in equal measure.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Maria: <i>She brings justice to those who deserve it, and feeds her own needs while doing so. I am glad to have her on our team.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Wash: <i>He knows that Truth is not always something most desire. Sometimes, perhaps often, it brings tears. But it is a worthy seeking regardless. I am glad to have cast down one of those \u201cHuntsman\u201d that sought him.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ms. Morte: <i>Sorcerers haven\u2019t changed in any age. So much power and knowledge, used all too often to satisfy transient desires. She has such potential, if only she can move herself past her own sense of boredom.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Anton: <i>We are both haunted by our pasts\u2026 though in your case, you have adopted others\u2019. I am, perhaps, thankful I cannot remember much of my own dead - this city and my thoughts are crowded enough.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bill: <i>In the time of Irem we helped the Shan-iatu move the stars themselves\u2026 I think. I hope now none were using them, especially worthies such as \u201cBill\u201d. He knows the value of holding to one\u2019s role, be it in society or Fate. And when, perhaps, it should be denied...</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Jiller: <i>The good doctor\u2019s obsession with the mind dwarfs any I have known. I sometimes wish I could answer his questions better, but even those I understand, I can\u2019t recall the details to answer them properly.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Norwood: <i>It never changes - those born thinking they are entitled to a key spot on the Scroll. His mind is clouded by his own imagined glories. Still, in others he seeks the value beneath the skin. He would have made a fine member of the Mesen-Nebu, I think.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Warner: <i>A seemingly simple boy hiding a terror from ancient times. But he\u2026 he seeks only to serve, both truth and his master, Norwood. He almost puts lie to the terrible memories I can nearly recall of his Tribe.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Alejandro: <i>He sought Justice in life and this has not changed in death. Though prone to anger more than many, I think he may be due that. Sometimes I even envy his freedom, if not his Lifelessness.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Janet: <i>A Relic that\u2026 thinks? Lives, of itself? She is not Lifeless, yet lacks true Life. Still, she seeks it. Truly one of the wonders that gladden my Ab.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Elliot: <i>The surgeon has helped many of our members, and for that alone he has my thanks. He has even patched me up once, and is welcome to uncover whatever he thinks he can with his instruments. But if I ever find he starts talking to LDI...</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">GG: <i>This one is an irritation. Thankfully, few consider her rants plausible. But sooner or later, she will speak of things not meant to be spoken.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Vera: <i>Full of fire and fury. She doesn\u2019t know that all it leaves is ashes, despite her deserving targets. And there may come a point where her foes\u2019 own crimes no longer outweigh hers.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Albrecht: <i>Arrogant, prideful, hungry - and not only for stolen blood. A tool of the Devourer, even though he preys upon the other Lifeless. So long as he keeps out of our way, he can linger a bit longer.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Landen: <i>I feel the local civic leader has darker plans than he lets on. Though he seems agreeable, even friendly enough in every encounter I\u2019ve had of him, and though I sense no urging from Bastu, I can\u2019t help but stay wary of him.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Friday on others:</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ishaq: <i>When we first started this partnership, it was during a rough time for me and more \u201cany port in a storm\u201d. But Ishaq has turned this into a home. Not since the Machine have I felt more \u201cwhere I belonged\u201d. Anything I can do for him and the agency, is not nearly enough compared to what they have done for me.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Gabby: <i>One of our first \u201cextra-normal\u201d hires and one of our best, in my professional opinion. My personal one, too - she even tries to get me to lighten up. I just wish she wasn\u2019t </i><b><i>quite</i></b><i> so inquisitive - I\u2019m still a bit sensitive about sharing secrets.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Maria: <i>I don\u2019t like her. I don\u2019t get her obnoxious exclusionism for \u201ckin\u201d, nor her hypocrisy towards not letting her prey get away with things she\u2019d excuse \u201ckin\u201d for. Still, I can\u2019t fault her effectiveness, or her dedication to the rest of the agency. So long as she keeps her hunger under control and doesn\u2019t betray us, I\u2019ll render her what assistance is needed.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Wash: <i>His surveillance skills are an incredible asset, and his professional dedication is indisputable. We\u2019re both looking over our shoulders for hunters, though he\u2019s at least learned to live a little more.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ms. Morte: <i>We\u2019re both addicted to mysteries, though her\u2019s are more focused around morbid topics. I\u2019m just glad she\u2019s too busy convincing herself things aren\u2019t worth her time to pry into my secrets.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Anton: <i>A very useful and lucrative contact. He possesses a wealth of information on those cases involving murder or suicide, and a wealth of funds to cover our retainer.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bill: <i>His contacts and understanding of the criminal underworld is an invaluable help to our organization. Especially since his compensation is so cheap. I should see about giving him some advice on blending in better some time.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Jiller: <i>His enthusiasm for delving into the workings of the mind is admirable, if a bit alarming. Especially considering his previous stated interest in the God-Machine. I may have to double up observation on him.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Norwood: <i>Clueless. If it wasn\u2019t for his being able to keep Warner stable and directed, we probably would have never hired him. Though he has proven useful for spinning events toward a more mundane explanation.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Warner: <i>Despite his puppy-like demeanor around Norwood, he is his own person, and possesses a keen intellect himself. But behind that shy, self-conscious, dishevelled exterior lurks something </i>terrifying<i>. Thankfully, Norwood keeps it contained by his very nature, and gives Warner something more productive to do than devastating the city, breaking minds, and forming bloody cults.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Alejandro: <i>A bit temperamental, but that is to be expected with a Savage Kindred. And he\u2019s perceptive, too - I\u2019m nearly certain that he hasn\u2019t penetrated my Cover, but he still knows something is up. If only he\u2019d work with the other detectives better and stop changing his address. Payroll is annoying enough as it is.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Janet: <i>I </i><b><i>knew</i></b><i> we should have done inventory earlier. Still, despite the security risk, I\u2019m glad we have her. Our systems have been outdated for years, and we are still somewhat deficient in our electronic expertise. Also\u2026 I\u2019m happy she finally has a bit of \u201cfreedom\u201d of her own.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Elliot: <i>Useful. I don\u2019t normally get out into physical conflicts much, but it is good to know there is someone who won\u2019t ask troubling questions when medical attention is needed. And I\u2019ll admit, I was curious if he could find anything in his \u201csample\u201d.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">GG: <i>Security threat - high priority. My contacts and analysis have reduced the likely identity to \u201cRicki Hargrave\u201d, \u201cGunda Mueller\u201d, \u201cDaniel Hubert\u201d, or \u201cIdella Beck\u201d. I could call in that \u201cHero\u201d my contacts gave me to confirm the source\u2026 but that would involve unacceptable risk to Maria. No.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Vera: <i>Dangerous variable. My plants within her organization report that their targets are outside the agency\u2019s typical subjects of value. Despite her destabilizing influence, she has her uses. And she is often good for business.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Albrecht: <i>Security threat - low. His predations upon the local vampires is as amusing as it is infuriating to them. So long as my sources report he hasn\u2019t turned his predations upon Alejandro, no further action is warranted. Beyond \u201cleaking\u201d the plots of further assaults against him to his contacts, that is.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Landen: <i>Dangerous unknown. He manipulates societies and people with skill towards plans even we have no idea of. And he makes it seem like the best idea in the world while doing so.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Gabby on others:</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ishaq: <i>Old Ishaq. I\u2019m happy he didn\u2019t let my reputation tar my chances at working here - the paycheck is handy and you wouldn\u2019t believe how expensive an all meat diet can get. Besides the particulars, he\u2019s a great boss, despite \u201csleeping\u201d most of the time and being an ancient undead horror. A great guy too, once he can remember what century it is. </i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Friday: <i>Ms Secretary, more like. Seriously though, she keeps the place together and running, especially with all of us &quot;personalities&quot;. I keep trying to get her to open up and not be so focused on the job. I even caught a rare glimpse of one of her honest smiles </i></span></span><i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">once.</span></span></i><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Maria: <i>Ex cop, which isn't usually my cup of tea, you know? But Maria's alright - she doesn't give me a hard time just to throw her weight around. And man, that one time we cornered that crooked accountant, he was practically sweating confessions and dirty secrets.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Wash: </span></span><i>He always trots out that put upon &quot;you won't like the truth&quot; spiel, even though he knows that doesn't dissuade anyone that comes to him in the first place. I think that's the point, really - he enjoys the &quot;I told you so&quot;. He also looks after me, which is sweet, but I can handle myself.</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ms. Morte: <i>When the bodies turn up without reasonable (or </i>too<i> reasonable) cause of death, she's your girl. You gotta make it weird enough to be worth her time, or her bored sighs will adjust the air pressure. Or help her out with Spirit business so she doesn't have to.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Anton: <i>The ghost guy. I investigated some of the shadows in his past once, but never found anything on him. The people he was competing with, however... that took me </i>days<i> to write up all their dirty business.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bill: </span></span><i>He's an odd one. Smells kinda funny too. He's great for picking up a trail though, and he's loves those cookies so much it's fun to talk to him.</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Jiller: <i>He's kinda creepy, in an asks weird questions kind of way. Not too bad a guy though - he wants to find out the truth too, just the </i>why<i> as opposed to the </i>how<i>. I try to bring him new interviewees from time to time after I've drained them of info.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Norwood: <i>The &quot;gentleman&quot;. It's hilarious the kinds of mental gymnastics he goes through to normalize the weird shit he encounters. I wonder how many news sources have people like him to sanitize the crap for the TV audience.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Warner: </span></span><i>He's not too bad, apart from the smell - he's so self conscious though, I'd never bring it up. I can tell he's really shy, and doesn't really know how to interact with others. I try to keep him in the loop, just so he knows there's someone there who talks to him and cares.</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Alejandro: </span></span><i>I like him - he doesn't take crap, or peddle BS to others. He finds out juicy stories like a fly finds meat. It's cute how he thinks he can shake me when I tail him too. I don't think he realizes I let him see me half the time.</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Janet: <i>Her marks were the same kind of people I targeted before. She can hunt out their dirty secrets online, and I'll find the evidence in meat-space - teamwork. I wish she'd hang out in person, but I understand why she can't.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Elliot: <i>Good guy. I don't often need help after a scrape, but how was I supposed to know that fence was silver tipped? All he asked for was a few tissue samples - thankfully the Lunacy doesn't work through blood samples. I meet up with him to trade questions some time - even if he doesn't say anything specific, you can get feel for what is going on just by who his clientele have been lately.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">GG: <i>She's never written about me. Figures - even the gossips won't publish my stories anymore. I wonder if that will change once I find out who and where she is though.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Vera: </span></span><i>Ole &quot;Kill it with fire&quot; Vera. I'd like her more if the bodies didn't pile up so high and she didn't treat my exposes as a hunting dog. I don't care if that warehouse was storing drugs - the firefighters have enough to worry about without you giving the arson spirits so many free meals, girl.</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Albrecht: <i>Rich bastard. He might not be the one trafficking those bodies, but he's cut from the same &quot;too-good-for-rules&quot; cloth. One of these days he's going to slip up and give me the dirt for a story he won't be able to cover up anymore.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Landen: <i>I worked a story once about one of his \u201cassociates\u201d before. He likes to keep at least 3 degrees of separation between him and anything dirty, and makes his tools think it was their own idea besides. The one time I\u2019ve cornered him for a scoop, he talked around me in circles. I feel like he found out more about me than I did of him. </i>Definitely<i>, bringing help next time.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Anton on others:</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ishaq: </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Friday: </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Gabby: </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Maria: </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Wash: </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ms. Morte: </span></span><i>A coroner and a necromancer, I hold her in mixed regard. One the one hand, her kind have been known to flagrantly abuse the dead. On the other, she has a career of making sure the dead see justice. I will judge her on her own merits, once I see more.</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bill: <i>An odd one. He seems nervous about me for reasons I do not know. Perhaps it has something to do with the strange mortality that surrounds him.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Jiller: <i>The doctor is oddly obsessed. And he seems to think I can whistle up any of the world's dead to answer his prodding questions.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Norwood: </span></span><i>He's patronized my casino from time to time and helped with a few cases. He refuses to believe in ghost, or anything supernatural, despite his experiences - far be it from be to disillusion him. Despite his manner, he </i>is<i> kind to others, regardless of means or appearance.</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Warner: </span></span><i>I've seen the young man hanging around Mr. Hart. He keeps quiet, so I'm not sure what to make of him personally.</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Alejandro: <i>A great help on making sure the dead get justice. My only regret is that he will never know peace and justice himself.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Janet: </span></span><i>Some of my patrons fell victim to her schemes when she was a tool, and others have benefited from her talents now that she is on her own. I think she understands what it means to pay back debts.</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Elliot: <i>I've heard about him and the things he does. Good for him - there is far enough death plaguing this city.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">GG: </span></span><i>A petty soul who thinks airing out others secrets makes them better. I wouldn't mind, if her writings gave more voice to the dead.</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Vera: <i>The dead hardly need more company, child, but I understand why you do what you do. Just please try to keep the casualties to a minimum.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Albrecht: <i>A vicious, sadistic dilettante who pretends to be something other than a monster. I've seen some of his victims. If I were younger, there would be a reckoning. </i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Landen: </span></span><i>The Alderman is a friend to whoever he talks to - even if that means being two or more people at once. Still, none of the Ghosts I've talked to have ever blamed him for any of their misfortunes. Convenient, I think. </i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 05-04-2017, 07:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T21:14:46-07:00","id":894547,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Siobhan Malloy</u> (Changeling, Grimm <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1elqCKhNJweqnLuUy8Rbh2PiZSsnccnXQWrNy8cPf5o4/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1\" target=\"_blank\">Spelldrinker</a>/Woodblood)</b><br /> <i>&quot;Oh, yeah. This definitely has the hallmarks of magic, alright.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Originally from Quebec, Siobhan has been aware of the World of Darkness ever since she was a child. Her family was touched with supernatural talents for generations, and even claimed remote descent to the Sisters of the Mountain, a Proximi Dynasty based in the Appalachian Mountains. While this ancestry led to their association with the local Mysterium, and even resulted in a few Proximi coming up on their family tree, this became an object of resentment for her when she did not manifest overt supernatural gifts, and was shunned by most of her extended family for it.<br /> <br /> When her younger sister was discovered to be a Proximus, herself, it was the last straw for the woman. She cut ties with her family as soon as she graduated high school, and moved to Toronto in order to enroll in a university and start fresh. She also sought to further distance herself from her old life by refusing to have anything to do with the supernatural. This was not easy for her, as Toronto was rife with supernatural occurrences, especially those tied to the local freehold of Changelings.<br /> <br /> Siobhan eventually began building up a career as a journalist after graduating. She still tried to keep herself firmly entrenched in the mundane world, but her Sleepwalker status and the nature of some of the stories she pursued invariably kept drawing her back to the life she left behind. Things began to escalate when her sister - who had, by then, Awakened to the Lunargent Thorn - tried to protect her from a supernatural threat to her life. Sadly, Siobhan's refusal of her help and her continued denial of the World of Darkness ended with her being spirited away by her Keeper, while her sister was left near death.<br /> <br /> The journalist's memories of her time in Arcadia were fragmented, moreso than those of other Changelings. But she nearly came close to breaking in her durance when she finally realized that escape was only possible through the occult lore she had long condemned. She struggled to recall the folk tales and superstitions that her family observed, drawing on them for reference as she observed her captor and his domain for an opportunity to free herself. Eventually, she discovered and exploited a particular Frailty of her Keeper's, and used his subsequent moment of weakness to make a dash for the Hedge. She escaped back to Toronto, but soon learned that a great deal of time had passed in her absence. This left her devastated, and the fact that she could find nothing on her sister's survival only drove the guilt deeper.<br /> <br /> At present, Siobhan has largely come to terms with her changed existence. She had gone on to join the Jade Court, drawn as she was to its dedication to preserving the stories told to ensure the freehold's prosperity. Eventually, she became recognized as one of the Court's Ministers for her work as an envoy to other cities and a researcher for new stories to be added to the libraries.<br /> <br /> It was in this capacity that she came into contact with members of the IE Agency, when they became involved in an incident that threatened her motley's efforts in setting up an embassy for the freehold in the city. The case's conclusion soon led to the creation of a partnership, wherein the changelings (including the Grimm herself) may be called in as consultants for a given case in exchange for the Agency stepping in to assist them as some of their regular clients. The fact that their own outpost happens to double as a shop for rare antiques and books has also put them in the graces of certain individuals.<br /> <br /> To most people, Siobhan appears to be a young woman of Irish descent, with dark hair and fair skin. Her dark green eyes have a sharpness to them honed from a career of journalism and the circumstances that led to her escape. She also has tattoos in the shape of abstract symbols adorning various parts of her body.<br /> <br /> This appearance is her Mask, however. And those who can see past it instead behold a real-life wood nymph, with green moss-like hair and skin with the look and feel of tree bark. The tattoos, meanwhile, become some sort of runic script, and people get the impression that they're the incantation for some sort of protection spell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://cache2.asset-cache.net/gc/169055609-portrait-of-girl-with-long-dark-hair-gettyimages.jpg?v=1&amp;c=IWSAsset&amp;k=2&amp;d=dRh6D7ghdJcpEjlGnTs%2FXPQ3umWFMXq4VO4dlJect8ZtJJSqE5aGWMZmQXtG%2BnMP\" target=\"_blank\">Face Cast</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>Outtakes from Siobhan</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Ishaq: </b>&quot;I rarely see him, in person. But a few of the times that I did happened at the store, especially when one of our curios turned out to be an item of interest to him.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Friday: </b>&quot;I know who she is. Or, rather, what she is. But I'm not telling you anything. She's got her reasons for hiding behind Masks, and they're not too different from my own&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Gabby:</b> &quot;We have a complicated rapport. Sometimes we work together, and other times we compete with each other. It really depends on the story we're chasing. But I'm pretty sure she hasn't lived down how I used one of her <i>own</i> tricks against her the last time we met up&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Maria:</b> &quot;A good cop, even though she's long been out of her police blues. But even so, I'm not letting down my guard around her. I've seen her real form while roaming through the dreams&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Wash:</b> &quot;I don't know whether I should like him or hate him. He's got my respect for being willing to dig up the truth, no matter how ugly it is. But he's a lot like some guys I knew in both the Brass and Silver Courts back in Toronto. And most of them ended up dead or worse thanks to the Others&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Ms. Morte:</b> &quot;I used to have trouble dealing with Mages before I was taken. They kept reminding me of how I wasn't so special compared to my sister. Nowadays, I <i>still</i> can't stand them. But this time, it's because they just can't ignore a Mystery that's in front of them even when it's more trouble than it's worth. Morte's an exception in some cases. She knows when to <i>not</i> pry into something. Plus, she's a good friend of someone in my motley&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Anton:</b> &quot;He's truly a man of his word. He keeps in mind all the debts he has with the ghosts he caters to, and I've even sent a few Lost his way knowing that he might help them find closure. He certainly did for me when I asked him to join me down at Quebec so he could give me a chance to say goodbye to my parents&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Bill:</b> &quot;I'm not quite sure what to make of him. But he seems friendly enough, and he doesn't ask for much if you need his help&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Jiller:</b> &quot;He's Mad, I tell you. Or getting there, at least. I swear he'd fit right in with the Others if he didn't exercise such restraint&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Norwood and Warner:</b> &quot;It's like how it is with Changelings and Faetouched. Only reversed. And I can't help but think that this partnership's not as equal as those two think it is&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Aldo: </b>&quot;I can sympathize with him for what he went through. And if it's any consolation, at least it didn't take too long for him to open his eyes to all the crap going on around him&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Janet:</b> &quot;I actually ran into her in person, once. A changeling with a habit of hunting down fetches on sight apparently mistook her for one, and my motley made the split-second decision to help her. It turned out well in the end. She keeps us updated on what's going down in the city, and I go out of my way to give her a hand in figuring out some steps in her Pilgrimage&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Elliot: </b>&quot;While I don't deny that people like him are invaluable, he puts himself at great risk wanting to know more about the darker secrets of the world. Sooner or later, he might end up becoming one of the very things he studies&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>GG:</b> &quot;I think someone needs to dig up gossip on<i> her</i> for a change. Because she has no idea just how much trouble her work can cause&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Vera: </b>&quot;She reminds me of a Bridge Burner I know who used similar methods. And I have a feeling she'll end up going overboard just like he did. For now, though, we're keeping track of her work from a distance&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Johnathon: </b>&quot;Some of the children he cares for are special, one way or another. And he reaches out to us whenever he requires our services to care for them&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Albrecht:</b> &quot;He needs to be dealt with sooner or later. It's only a matter of time before he starts craving for more than just vampire blood&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 05-26-2016, 09:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T07:45:51-07:00","id":894714,"title":"","content":"Hmm.. A Offering as a Contact/Client (Potentially)<br /> <br /> <b><u>Johnathon Nicolls</u> (Purified)</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;The mind of a child is a wonderful thing, they should be protected and respected. As they are the future we should strive to create...&quot;<br /> &quot;There once was a Legion, It marched to war, leaving the children to weep. There once was a Legion... and the children Feasted.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> A short chubby man who is constantly smiling, his brown hair is kept in a ponytail. When he speaks his soft voice is reassuring and calm, never demeaning.<br /> <br /> Johnathon maintains a children's home for lost and Orphaned children, Officially that is all he does, Unofficially he takes care of children that are stuck in between states or who's families would be harmful for them to be around and vice versa, if the child is to dangerous for the parents to look after he will ensure they are safe and receive all the care and Teaching they require.<br /> Long ago he was a roman legionnaire who stumbled upon the Horrors of Rome and it Broke him... he found himself unable to fight for the city anymore. It took the death of a child in his arms to snap him back into the world of the living, forcing him to fight for the defense of something that didn't have a concept of nation or worldly goods, only an innocence that was far to precious to see wiped from the world.<br /> <br /> Since then he has decided that the world needs caretaker's for the innocent and if no-one else would he will. Sometime though-out the Ages he became a Purified and developed an intense Anger at Vampires (He doesn't want to talk about it, but the details seem to include him meeting the Children's Crusade and learning to care for atleast some of them before they were hunted down and killed.) and has moved from city to city over many ages, Changing his name and Opening a new home for children. He rarely gets angry, however never threaten his children.... He will find a Way to Hurt you just as much as you have hurt the child.<br /> <br /> <i>Knowledge:</i> Has a working knowledge on most of the supernaturals and an intense dislike of Vampires, even if he does realize it is irrational and that none of the current generation of Vampires are to blame for the things that happened to the Children's Crusade. He has some contacts in the City with each of the Supernatural elements and uses them to insure his children are left alone or given the right care for their needs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T14:43:06-07:00","id":895017,"title":"","content":"And now for a whole 'nother thing!<br /> Okay, maybe not so different.<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b><u>Rachum (Demon)</u></b><br /> He has no past, no story behind him, no nothing. He just stumbled upon the town one day, traumatized like no Demon ever should possibly be, a sobbing, mumbling wreck, wandering the streets, until one of the friendlier Unchained in the town (A Guardian Integrator going by Monsieur Papillon) picked him up. He tried to help him, comfort him, other stuff, but ulitmately, the reasons behind what happened to him were left uncovered except for a vague mention of &quot;Sydney&quot;. He only ever seemed to stop being curled up in a corner mumbling nonsensical words to himself at the mention of crimial activity, especially organized crime. When the issue came up, he stoped being a mental shipwreck, and instead became an ingenious investigator, using his analytic mind, sharp wit and incredible investigative abilities to crack open the crime like a nut, pick it apart, piece by piece and bring it to justice. Usually Vera's justice, beacause she's the one that M. Papillon had most contact with. And after the case was out of the way, Rachum again curled up in a corner, rocking back and forth. Papillon ultimately decided that he should do something about such a great detective, and decided to see if the IE would hire him. They did. Now, Rachum just sort of stumbles around the third plan, being a nervous wreck he still is, and only springing back up when there's a case issued to him. He is very fond, and very specialized in gangs, mafia and other forms of organized crime though...<br /> There's a reason for that...<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> And that is that Rachum is not entirely the nervous wreck of a Demon that sits a couple hours mumbing in his office every other day and then disappears into... Somewhere, that people in the IE don't even seem to notice unless they have buisness to him.<br /> Instead, he's one of the most diabolical criminal masterminds in the city... Meet Akzari!<br /> <b><u>Akzari (Demon, Messenger/Analyst(I have not yet decided) Tempter)</u></b><br /> Akzari, ever since his Fall, was greatly consumed by the idea of creating a perfect political construct, an empire perfectly balanced, unable to be scatched by any sort of external foe or internal conflict, an empire to prevail for all times, where all the cogs and the wheels were turning, turning more precisely than the most precise of Infrastructure. And all that, without a single bit of Influence from the Machine. Throught the centuries, he tried different approaches. He engaged in great politics, he established small cults, he tried to create colonies. But it all failed. Failed miserably. But a long time ago, he found a new mean to do just what he wants, to achieve Hell. Organized Crime. He joined the mob as a serial lawyer, one of the army that the Verazone Crime Family had on their payroll. And soon enough, through impressive game of covers, lies, and deciet, he managed to achieve the status of don Verazone's trusted consigliere, and the gray eminence in one of the most powerful men in the town's underground. Ruthless, cruel, calculative, prefect tactitian, skilled politician, with no moral qualms whatsoever about reating his perpetuum mobile of human minds, working in the light and shadow, Akzari has managed to practically get monopoly on every shady activity in the city, all the strings leading to his hands, an absolute ruler and a machine that couldn't be brought down. That's when Ishaq and his cult came into the equation. And everything went to hell in a handbasket. In no-time, the influences the Arisen had amongst the few &quot;Pure&quot; people in the Vampire covenants, changeling courts, police, everywhere, with Ishaq's help and at the payroll of a shady individual with seemingly unlimited budget managed to bring all the establishment down to the state we see it at today. Akzari was by no means depraved of his power, but the Vampires he kept in his pocket had spilled out, the policemen on his payroll decided to quit working for him, the Changeling courts undertook major restructurization and the new rulers knew better, the Consilium, under the pressure of all the others , invited Free Council who torn it apart and rebuild in the matter of a single year, and the other groups he exterminated with extreme prejudice came back, lustful for revenge. Akzari holds the grudge against whoever hired Ishaq for the job to bring down his empire to this day. And the shadowy figure seems to still be a constant client, making the Illuminated Eye a thorn in his side. But, as he realized, he could use his nemesis' tool to do his own bidding, slowly getting rid of inconvenient elements and rivaling groups... And that's exactly what he is doing...<br /> <br /> Akzari's opinions:<br /> Ishaq: <i>It;s nothing personal, its about your client. Even if noone outside of you knows who he is and you don't even remember. Either way, I saw some of your tricks you threaten people with. They're mine now.</i><br /> IE as a whole: <i>It needs to be eradicated. ASAP. </i><br /> GG: <i>I'm still one of the secrets he has yet to uncover. It pleases me that I'm the only one not dimwitted enough to get picked apart by a third-rate gossip blogger. This means I'm still superior to everyone else in this town. </i><br /> Vera: <i>An useful tool, if blunt. Just point her to a target and let off the leash, and the job is done.</i><br /> Albrecht: <i>Was here before I came, will be when I'm done. I keep to my niche, he keeps to his. Can't deny he's a very useful ally to have though.</i><br /> Landen: <i>A prime example of what the chaos caused by my shadowy opponent has left in it's wake. </i><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11117,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","user":"Inquisitor","date":". 05-20-2016, 05:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T03:42:55-07:00","id":896673,"title":"","content":"Have you got a street-level homeless contact yet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T07:10:10-07:00","id":896774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hastur00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/865489-crossover-concept-detective-agency?p=896673#post896673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you got a street-level homeless contact yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe Bill (the Alien)? Though he has more general crime contacts. And he isn't exactly homeless. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9065-darkblade\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9065\" data-vbnamecard=\"9065\">Darkblade</a>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T11:35:19-07:00","id":897013,"title":"","content":"Bill is effectively playing the same game that <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Landen is. He understands the systems of society. The key difference being that he feels he belongs on the bottom and any efforts he takes to fix society must come from there. Technically speaking he lives in his vessel which is hidden in an overgrown abandoned lot on the outskirts but for most intents and purposes he is homeless.<br /> <br /> That said a more traditional homeless contact would be welcome.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9065-darkblade","name":"Darkblade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T13:57:04-07:00","id":897151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkblade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/865489-crossover-concept-detective-agency?p=897013#post897013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said a more traditional homeless contact would be welcome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Crud, what I've got is way too close to Bill already. NVM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T14:08:13-07:00","id":897166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hastur00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/865489-crossover-concept-detective-agency?p=897151#post897151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crud, what I've got is way too close to Bill already. NVM.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. What about highlighting the differences?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T17:57:19-07:00","id":899591,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/865489-crossover-concept-detective-agency?p=894547#post894547\">Finally finished up my write-up for Siobhan</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T19:05:08-07:00","id":900549,"title":"","content":"Here's a story hook for an upcoming character I'll be posting. A Guardian/Saboteur Unchained who has a history with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3981_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3981\" data-vbnamecard=\"3981\">RickmanUK</a>'s Purified character, both as an Angel <i>and</i> a Demon. <hr /><br /> &quot;Police are still scrambling to investigate the particularly brutal murder of a couple whose son went missing at around the same time. But the local Unchained know that one of their own was the killer. They suspect that the boy may be the Cover of another Demon, but those Inquisitors and Integrators who have been monitoring the hunter-angels that appeared in the wake of the murder have noticed that they're only pursuing the murderer. Is the boy another Unchained? Or something else? The only one who might be able to offer an answers might be a new Guardian who has just arrived. And he seems to be racing against a clock to find the kid&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T21:39:10-07:00","id":900671,"title":"","content":"Here's the one character asked for but no one has delivered on, but I have to admit he isn't the least bit original.<br /> 'Mr.' Hawk: (Mage/Obrimos/Arrow/Perfected Adept)<br /> There's one word to describe Hawk; Intimidating. He's big, black, bald, with a smile and laugh that reek predatory contempt. His role at the agency is the obvious 'big stick', he intimidates people the old fashion way. Sometimes that's all it takes to get someone to spill their secrets and when that doesn't work out...he shakes people up and people like that tend to lash out in reckless ways that often expose the very things they were trying to hide.<br /> It also helps that when things spill out in a violent mess he is a man capable of bringing down some heavy fire.<br /> Most people aren't surprised to learn that he spent time serving in the Army's special forces, they are surprised to learn it was as a field medic. Another useful skill to have when things go sideways.<br /> Hawk swore oaths to protect and those oaths define him. He is also experienced at working with a team and if he respects you, taking orders.<br /> If you haven't recognized him yet, just picture a thirty something Avery Brooks with a big gun.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T08:52:41-07:00","id":910109,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Micheal O'Neal / Calvaris</b></u> (Angel-Guardian, Rank 4, Exile)<br /> <i>&quot;I was about to retire...&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Chief Micheal O'Neal has served on the force diligently since his transfer a decade ago. Under his guidance, crime has ceased rising and unsolved cases have decreased. Though now occupying more of an administrative role, he still ventures out from time to time to back up new officers just getting their feet wet. He commands respect from the entire force, if not affection due to his being a stickler for the rules. To hear him say it, he's been close to retirement for years now, but still manages to be on the job each day.<br /> <br /> At least, that's what everyone human knows. The Angel known as Calvaris was placed by the God-Machine as head of the local law enforcement, ostensibly to keep proper order for one of Its other projects. It's just... that task seems to have concluded, yet Calvaris was never recalled. He sits in his role, Exiled, awaiting orders that never come, carrying out a mission that seems increasingly impossible without compromise. He's still nominally loyal to the Machine, but circumstances have forced him to adopt less... optimal choices and methods. He's cut deals with other Supernatural forces and looked the other way when it maintains his efforts toward secrecy. He's even dealt with the Unchained on occasion. Mostly, he just wants to keep order, make sure the supernatural is concealed, and the law is obeyed, roughly in that order.<br /> <br /> <b>Concepts and Ideas:</b> Angelic Police Chief, left in the cold. Guardian of the Masquerade. Defender of Law and Order, even as he is forced to compromise it.<br /> <br /> <b>Secrets: </b>He's assembled dossiers of those he's identified in preparation for he return... but he's also contracted alternative Covers, in the event he finally Falls. Even he doesn't know how to resolve the apparent implications of betrayal in line with his professed loyalist position, and grow agitated if it is brought up.<br /> Knows the IE Detective Agency has Unchained, but doesn't know who they are.<br /> <br /> <b>Calvaris on others:</b><br /> Ishaq: <i>The old man himself. In my missions, I've rarely encountered these ancient servitors of the long dead Empire, but in those cases, they've rarely turned out to be as... banal, as Ishaq appears to be. I'd almost like him, if he wasn't harboring Renegades amongst his ranks.</i><br /> Gabby: <i>An annoying nuisance, mostly. Always asking questions, even when some of them shouldn't be asked in public. </i><br /> Maria: <i>She used to be such a good cop, but then she let her anger and her Hunger get the better of her. We can't stoop to those levels and still expect to keep order and respect.</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ms. Morte: <i>A highly talented coroner, and an asset to the force. I suspect her bored, too-good-for-this attitude will keep her from climbing very high on the promotional ladder, though. A pity, though that won't stop me from sending some of the harder work her way.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Jiller: </span></span><i>The doctor is a nut - but a scary one. His obsession is peculiar on its own, but combined with his broken theories on criminal behavior, most just dismiss him. They're ignoring just how often he turns out to be </i>right<i>, even if his logic is a bit... unusual.</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Norwood: <i>He's a pompous twit, but oddly successful. As long as he remains as clueless as the rest of the city, I'm not going to complain about the cases he resolves.</i><br /> Janet: <i>As if we didn't have enough to worry about, now we've got some self-aware chat-bot engaging in cyber-crime.</i><br /> Jonathan: <i>As long as he keeps out of the spotlight, he's welcome to steward the lost waifs he collects. He just better make sure they keep their noses clean and don't end up in juvy</i></span></span>.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Vera: </span></span><i>A chaotic, lawless element to be eliminated at the earliest opportunity. If only I could get the budget to afford to do so.</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Albrecht: <i>He hides behind lawyers and connections, but with his predilections, sooner or later he's going to trip up and leave evidence he can't worm out of. Then he's </i>mine<i>.</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Landen: <i>The alderman likes his plots and plans kept out of sight. It's amusing to think he can complete with the true Architect. As long as he doesn't make a scene, he's welcome to spin whatever little schemes he can come up with for the Machine to turn to Its favor.</i><br /> Akzari: </span></span><i>One of the most dangerous Renegades in the city. It took me months to root out his corruption from my police force. I know some of my peers think he's </i><i>been destroyed, but I've seen his influence moving in the shadows still.</i><i> Maybe bringing him in will get the Machine's attention...</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 06-22-2016, 10:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T17:32:38-07:00","id":919400,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a>: I'd like to add <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/913049-beast-detective?p=919388#post919388\"><b>Quon Li</b></a>. His personality isn't very well developed at the moment, as I wrote him in 1 hour for Wyrdhamster. I figure he would be quite a good listener and practical, but arrogant and greedy. He is upfront about this greed though, and while he prefers to have few partners, he can co-operate to a fair extent. He also has a lot of money for a detective and several magic items, which he is really good at using as leverage. Your thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T19:19:50-07:00","id":919447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/865489-crossover-concept-detective-agency?p=919400#post919400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a>: I'd like to add <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/913049-beast-detective?p=919388#post919388\"><b>Quon Li</b></a>. His personality isn't very well developed at the moment, as I wrote him in 1 hour for Wyrdhamster. I figure he would be quite a good listener and practical, but arrogant and greedy. He is upfront about this greed though, and while he prefers to have few partners, he can co-operate to a fair extent. He also has a lot of money for a detective and several magic items, which he is really good at using as leverage. Your thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Interesting... how do you see him working with the agency's existing Anakim?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T05:57:33-07:00","id":919666,"title":"","content":"JOHN GRANGER (Hunter/Sin-Eater)<br /> I originally built John to be super-investigation focused. He's got all the great investigative merits: Eidetic Memory, Professional Training (Detective), Trained Observer, Patience, Good Time-Management, etc. However, the stories he wound up in forced him to develop more combat capability. After five years of playing him, he was basically a superhero. He even picked up that Combat Archery merit from the Hurt Locker preview, and can now reliably bow-stake multiple vampires in a single action. Eventually, he nearly died and became a Sin-Eater. The main powers he uses from that are the increased resilience, the Pyre-Flame Shroud (he loves putting the fear into vampires by bursting into flame during a fight), and his Keystone which is a (souped up by his Geist back when it was human) WWII motorcycle. He's kind of ridiculous, honestly, an insane mashup of Ghost Rider, Green Arrow, the Crow, Sherlock Holmes, and the Punisher.<br /> <br /> As for my favorite investigative anecdote: One time he was attempting to acquire intelligence on a high-profile vampire target's haven. The ST made it an extended action, with each roll representing an eighteen-hour day of investigation. Ok. So, Good Time Management let me cut the roll-time to nine hours, so I had plenty of time to rest and regain a Willpower after each roll. My base Intelligence + Investigation pool was nine, so Patience would give me 11 rolls. I used a Willpower on each roll for Professional Training to make it a Rote Action. The bonuses from equipment, Contacts, etc made my dice pool for each roll (even after accounting for penalties from the vampire's Haven merit) a total of 14. I shit you not, I rolled <b>100 successes</b>.<br /> <br /> The ST was blown away. He said, &quot;Ok, so the first 25 of those are an Exceptional Success of Exceptional Successes. You know everything there is to know about the building, its layout, its security, all of it. To represent that, and to save me the trouble of having to draw up a super detailed schematic of the place, the other 75 successes are bonus dice you can add to yours or anyone else's dice pool during the operation.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2573-inkpenavenger","name":"inkpenavenger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2573_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T16:49:23-07:00","id":920005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/865489-crossover-concept-detective-agency?p=919447#post919447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting... how do you see him working with the agency's existing Anakim?</div> </div> </div> </div> Marias is a physically powerful giantess who looks out for children and other people she sees as helpless, and she does this out of idealism. Quon wants to make sure the big guys know they can't just take whatever and whomever they want, but he does this mostly for his satisfaction, and to share stories with other supernaturals (which is when he suddenly gets a lot more talkative). He wants his Kin to know that there better ways to inspired respect than to make people disappear and keep secrets, and that there are things out who can do the same to them. They don't always listen, but Quon is patient. He knows some things always get lost, and that's when he can shed some light on the truth.<br /> <br /> So, I guess Marias is the sanguine idealist with a chip on her shoulder, while Quon is the choleric pragmatist who's in the business more for fun and profit. They probably would disagree often, but they would agree they can't just let supernaturals rule over mortals unchecked.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T00:03:09-07:00","id":947572,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Kenneth Trager</u> [Redeemed Alchemist, Formerly Osiran Mystic]</b><br /> - The IE Agency employs the services of a number of special people, and the man named Kenneth Trager is no exception. A social worker who is ocasionally called in as a consultant, he seems mundane apart from his interest in alchemy and the occult. Those who look deeper into his life (and met him in another) know that he has more intriguing origins.<br /> <br /> Kenneth was not born human, but instead came into the world gasping for breath at the shallows of a dark lake. He was once a Promethean, the result of an Ophidian's studies on the Divine Fire. And his Pilgrimage began the day he refused to join his creator in embracing the Refinement of Flux. He spent many years preparing for his Great Work, passing through different Refinements and Roles in his efforts to understand humanity. He became especially defined by his experiences as an Originist and Mystic, as he was exposed to the experiences of not only his fellow Created, but other supernaturals. In time, he formed a throng with several like-minded Prometheans, and explored much of the World of Darkness in their company.<br /> <br /> The Nepri's New Dawn came during what he recalls was his final confrontation with his creator. The Centimanus and his pack of Pandorans had been hunting the throng for weeks, and had already managed to kill two of their number. In order to allow his friends to live, Kenneth chose to hold off the pack and sacrifice himself by triggering a Firestorm. The resulting inferno also consumed the Pandorans and his mentor, and allowed his surviving throngmates to escape.<br /> <br /> It was sheer luck that enough of the Osiran's body remained for him to return to life. However, what would be his final Journey to the River would be the only time he came upon Anahita, The River of Life. And once he drank of its waters, he was revived not as a Promethean, but as a true human being.<br /> <br /> Kenneth's last resurrection left him with memories of the life built up by the Great Work. As a human, he was a quiet and introverted person who had been the only child of his family. He had spent a few years as an independent social worker before settling down at a job in a local school. Since then, he has come to be well-liked not only by the faculty for his dilligent work ethic, but also by the students for his genuine concern for their well-being. And if there was ever one quality of his that was considered eccentric, it was his fascination for the paranormal and supernatural.<br /> <br /> The Redeemed would remember his old life when he crossed paths with a Promethean at the school. He had noticed her coming to the library from time to time, browsing on the books and computers on one subject or another. But it was only when he decided to tail her one day that it would all come back to him, when he witnessed the Promethean be attacked by a Pandoran. She managed to put the creature down, but ended up flaring her Disfigurements upon drawing on her Pyros. Kenneth saw her briefly for what she was, and it stoked the lingering embers of his Azoth within him.<br /> <br /> Kenneth took a brief sabbatical following that encounter to properly sort out the memories that came back. He remembered everything: how he spent years as a reanimated corpse working to become human, and how he had finallly attained it after he died fighting the monster that once was his progenitor. He recalled other creatures like him who sought to do the same, and he knew that the woman he tried to follow was one of them.<br /> <br /> Other aspects of his prior existence slowly resurfaced. The former Nepri began sensing paranormal forces at work around him, and he could even affect them to an extent by focusing his will to invoke certain abilities. And as he further explored his old memories, Kenneth felt the need to give more meaning to his life, and to help his former fellows bring themselves closer to the Dawn. This eventually led him to the study of Azothic Alchemy.<br /> <br /> Unlike most Alchemists, Kenneth came to his craft with good intentions and experience from his past life. He does not wish to improve or transcend his humanity beyond the changes he already received. Instead, his studies are geared towards aiding any Created he encounters. He knows that mortality can be achieved, and is willing to lend a hand to a Promethean in deciphering the next step in his Great Work. The former Nepri's studies are also driven by personal reasons. He remembers having been part of a throng, and that he had left them behind after giving his life fighting his creator and subsequently achieving the New Dawn. He has worked to ascertain their whereabouts ever since, wanting to know whether or not they had succeeded as he had.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://i.istockimg.com/image-zoom/73872517/3/380/254/stock-photo-73872517-upset-mid-adult-man.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Face Cast</a><br /> <br /> <b>Notes:</b><br /> \u2022 Kenneth is an Alchemist of Magnitude 4, and has developed the following Distillations -- Strike the Heart, Biting Aura, Confession, Daybreak, Dazzling Corona, Outshining the Sun, Nameless, Safe Sojourn, Soothe, and Jolt.<br /> \u2022 Kenneth is one of the few Redeemed who retained a fragment of his original power. He can use the Veritas Alembic and its associated Distillations, using Willpower or Pyros to activate them. These do not count towards the number based on his Magnitude.<br /> \u2022 Kenneth suffers from the Sick Tilt when exposed to Flux-based creatures. Centimani and active Pandorans inflict the moderate version, whereas a Lilithim causes the grave version.<br /> \u2022 Failing certain Distillations causes the Degaussed Condition.<br /> \u2022 Kenneth experiences a limited form of Disquiet. Whenever he fails a Breaking Point roll, anyone in his presence must make a Disquiet roll, with an effective Azoth equal to [10 - the Alchemist's Integrity].<br /> \u2022 Kenneth's Milestone Refinements were Aurum, Plumbum, Argentum, and Phosphorum. His Milestone Roles were those of Companion, Follower, Chronicler, Pilgrim, Explorer, Daredevil, Psychopomp, Watcher, Envoy, and Observer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 08-10-2016, 11:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T06:38:00-07:00","id":947722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/865489-crossover-concept-detective-agency?p=947572#post947572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><u>Kenneth Trager</u> [Redeemed Alchemist, Formerly Osiran Mystic]</b><br /> - The IE Agency employs the services of a number of special people, and the man named Kenneth Trager is no exception. A social worker who is ocasionally called in as a consultant, he seems mundane apart from his interest in alchemy the occult. Those who look deeper into his life (and met him in another) know that he has more intriguing origins.</div> </div> </div> </div>Always happy to have more join the crew. How did Kenneth encounter the IE detective agency, or did they contact him?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T07:55:18-07:00","id":947773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/865489-crossover-concept-detective-agency?p=947722#post947722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Always happy to have more join the crew. How did Kenneth encounter the IE detective agency, or did they contact him?</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine they reached out to him first, seeing as he normally keeps a low profile to avoid attracting more unsavory Alchemists (and hunters). And I imagine they might not have been immediately aware he had supernatural talents until he was approached for questioning on a case concerning someone he likely knew or was at least acquainted with.<br /> <br /> On a semi-related note, seeing as his most favored Refinement as a Promethean was that of the Mystic, I can also picture Kenneth having picked up Merits that reflect his interest in the supernatural (like Deadpan and Ritual Savvy from Mage). Plus, I was thinking that some of his research might have allowed (or will eventually allow) him to develop a few Supernatural Merits to supplement his Distillations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T08:05:47-07:00","id":947782,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Kenneth's Outtakes</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Ishaq:</b> &quot;I can't help but think there's a link between the Nepri and these Deathless somehow. There are just too many similarities between them. Perhaps he knows something I don't?&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Friday:</b> &quot;She's polite with me, but she always keeps her distance whenever she comes to me for input. I have a feeling she knows what I can do, even though I've done my best to keep a low profile&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Gabby:</b> &quot;Oh, Gabrielle isn't bad company. She's only annoyed with me whenever she makes the mistake of using her powers while sneaking up on me. But really, she's harmless unless you've got a story for her.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Maria:</b> &quot;One of my good friends was a Beast like her, and he helped me keep to the Pilgrimage when I came close to stepping off. That only made it harder for me when I learned he gave up being human. May Miss Katsaros never fall into that fate&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Wash:</b> &quot;The truth might not be what you want, but it's almost always what you need. He understands that sentiment, at least.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Ms. Morte:</b> &quot;We have an understanding as research partners. She keeps me in the loop on Consilium affairs and provides me with certain reagents. In return, I give her whatever she needs to work her own magic. So far, I have no reason to regret this arrangement&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Anton:</b> &quot;It's funny how I'm still afraid of death, even after dying three times. I cannot help but be envious of him with how blaise he can normally be about it&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Bill:</b> &quot;I don't know what to make of him, really. He isn't human, and he certainly isn't anything I've ever seen before.<br /> <br /> <b>Jiller:</b> &quot;I know he's shown interest in Disquiet. But for my sake and everyone else's, I hope he never experiences it.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Norwood:</b> &quot;It's amazing how he can go about his life not believing in what lies in the shadows. If it weren't for his redeeming behavior towards Warner, I wouldn't be so tolerant of him.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Warner:</b> &quot;He's somewhat likeable, despite what kind of being he is. But I still observe him with a wary eye.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Aldo:</b> &quot;There was an old story I heard from a vampire I met. It spoke of a quest for mortality not unlike the Pilgrimage. Perhaps if he chose to walk that road, he might perhaps be free of his condition.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Janet:</b> &quot;She has a long road ahead of her. And I can only hope she finds the Dawn despite whatever hardships come her way.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Elliot:</b> &quot;He's still trying to understand just how a body reanimated by the Divine Fire can transform into a real person with a paper trail of history. But other than that, he's a good person to compare notes with.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Siobhan:</b> &quot;You can learn a great deal from the stories she collects. You just have to listen.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>GG:</b> &quot;I can understand <i>why</i> she goes digging for secrets. But some things are best left in the dark&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Vera:</b> &quot;She's a Firestorm waiting to happen. And when it finally hits, nothing be spared.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Albrecht:</b> &quot;He's only sticking to vampires, right now, but I've seen other Alchemists do what they do for the same reasons. If he starts dabbling in any way, he needs to be dealt with fast&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 08-14-2016, 12:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-15T06:02:36-07:00","id":1254468,"title":"","content":"Oh, Warner Roach is contributing to the &quot;In-Character&quot; discussion on the Princess Discord here: <a href=\"https://discordapp.com/channels/373054864789602304/487025840501293066\" target=\"_blank\">https://discordapp.com/channels/3730...25840501293066</a><br /> <br /> Respecting creator control, I'll reference others listed here but make no changes or definitive statements regarding characters not my own. If you want to join in, feel free.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 09-15-2018, 10:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}